{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FnVnX3qBQF8Sng963rZ2a2","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json\",\n  \"framework\": null,\n  \"buildCommand\": \"node scripts/scan.mjs\",\n  \"installCommand\": \"echo 'ai-hub has no dependencies'\",\n  \"outputDirectory\": \".\",\n  \"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false },\n  \"trailingSlash\": false,\n  \"redirects\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/(.*)\",\n      \"missing\": [{ \"type\": \"host\", \"value\": \"crosato-arcade.vercel.app\" }],\n      \"destination\": \"https://crosato-arcade.vercel.app/$1\",\n      \"permanent\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"headers\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/data/games.json\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/assets/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/lib/kit/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/lib/hub/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/lib/(three|rapier)/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=604800\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/games/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=600, stale-while-revalidate=604800\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/covers/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=600, stale-while-revalidate=604800\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n---CLAUDE.md\n# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\n---README-grep\n91:field instead (see *Extra metadata*), and the filename only sorts the folder.\n238:The first reads every game in full, about half a minute at two thousand games;\n348:  many games it leaves. A browser with no WebGPU is told how many of them need\n358:The hub as a console's home screen, for a TV and a controller. One game at a\n368:| | Keyboard | Controller |\n389:random games, like a console's attract mode.\n498:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n542:node scripts/retrofit.mjs pick --wave 1 > .cache/wave1.txt   # one build of each title: readable, no WebGPU needed; smallest first\n543:awk 'NR % 7 == 0' .cache/wave1.txt > .cache/pilot.txt        # a pilot of about thirty, small to large\n552:  (`hub-check --draws-only`), and spends nothing on one it can't: a WebGPU-only\n553:  game in a browser without WebGPU, even when its title screen shows. On a\n572:one. Run a pilot of about thirty varied games, read the pass rate and cost per\n574:for you: commit what passed in batches of about fifty.\n605:about half a minute from one game to the next, less when everyone is ready\n688:  works as before. The free project pauses after about a week without use;\n716:**Extra metadata** — `data/overrides.json`, keyed by slug, wins over anything\n842:  check3d.py      one 3D game in headless browsers, WebGL2 and WebGPU\n853:The games on the shared kit run on the same stack: three.js r186 with `WebGPURenderer`\n854:(WebGL2 when WebGPU is missing), loaded once from `lib/three` through an\n856:gamepad and touch input. `lib/kit/README.md` is the guide for porting or\n868:library shelf cut to the files games actually load (about 14,700 files in all,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"404a3866-8f06-4903-9fc0-167670de6510","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:18.969Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json\",\n  \"framework\": null,\n  \"buildCommand\": \"node scripts/scan.mjs\",\n  \"installCommand\": \"echo 'ai-hub has no dependencies'\",\n  \"outputDirectory\": \".\",\n  \"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false },\n  \"trailingSlash\": false,\n  \"redirects\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/(.*)\",\n      \"missing\": [{ \"type\": \"host\", \"value\": \"crosato-arcade.vercel.app\" }],\n      \"destination\": \"https://crosato-arcade.vercel.app/$1\",\n      \"permanent\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"headers\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/data/games.json\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/assets/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/lib/kit/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/lib/hub/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/lib/(three|rapier)/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=604800\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/games/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=600, stale-while-revalidate=604800\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"/covers/(.*)\",\n      \"headers\": [\n        { \"key\": \"Cache-Control\", \"value\": \"public, max-age=600, stale-while-revalidate=604800\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n---CLAUDE.md\n# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\n---README-grep\n91:field instead (see *Extra metadata*), and the filename only sorts the folder.\n238:The first reads every game in full, about half a minute at two thousand games;\n348:  many games it leaves. A browser with no WebGPU is told how many of them need\n358:The hub as a console's home screen, for a TV and a controller. One game at a\n368:| | Keyboard | Controller |\n389:random games, like a console's attract mode.\n498:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n542:node scripts/retrofit.mjs pick --wave 1 > .cache/wave1.txt   # one build of each title: readable, no WebGPU needed; smallest first\n543:awk 'NR % 7 == 0' .cache/wave1.txt > .cache/pilot.txt        # a pilot of about thirty, small to large\n552:  (`hub-check --draws-only`), and spends nothing on one it can't: a WebGPU-only\n553:  game in a browser without WebGPU, even when its title screen shows. On a\n572:one. Run a pilot of about thirty varied games, read the pass rate and cost per\n574:for you: commit what passed in batches of about fifty.\n605:about half a minute from one game to the next, less when everyone is ready\n688:  works as before. The free project pauses after about a week without use;\n716:**Extra metadata** — `data/overrides.json`, keyed by slug, wins over anything\n842:  check3d.py      one 3D game in headless browsers, WebGL2 and WebGPU\n853:The games on the shared kit run on the same stack: three.js r186 with `WebGPURenderer`\n854:(WebGL2 when WebGPU is missing), loaded once from `lib/three` through an\n856:gamepad and touch input. `lib/kit/README.md` is the guide for porting or\n868:library shelf cut to the files games actually load (about 14,700 files in all,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FnVnX3qBQF8Sng963rZ2a2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj97ahta1yZFdxbWdQYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MbnFa4xytbyeA31fKSgqtz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/round.js --jq '.content' | base64 -d | sed -n '140,330p'","description":"Read how a hub round is coordinated and ended"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8850,"cache_read_input_tokens":63454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8850},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"0b6e8363-9af0-480a-9ad8-7ed5ff899922","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:19.282Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj97aTkutTp7pCYQthwL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MbnFa4xytbyeA31fKSgqtz":{"command":"gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/round.js --jq '.content' | base64 -d | sed -n '140,330p'","description":"Read how a hub round is coordinated and ended"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016XC1HUkHos1xUBAPJiL7wx","type":"tool_result","content":"'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\n\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n  pad = navigator.getGamepads ? [...navigator.getGamepads()].find((p) => p && p.connected) || null : null;\n  padWas = padNow;\n  padNow = pad ? pad.buttons.map((b) => b.pressed) : [];\n  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n  if (pressed(PAD.options) && !padNow[PAD.create]) return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) {\n    if (pressed(PAD.up)) menuKey('ArrowUp');\n    if (pressed(PAD.down)) menuKey('ArrowDown');\n    if (pressed(PAD.cross)) menuKey('Enter');\n    if (pressed(PAD.circle)) toggleMenu();\n  } else if (padNow.some((b, i) => b && !padWas[i] && i !== PAD.create && i !== PAD.options)) gesture();\n}\nconst pressed = (b) => !!padNow[b] && !padWas[b];\n\n// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\nlet muted = false;\nconst menu = {\n  open: false,\n  at: 0,\n  items: [\n    { label: () => `Sound: ${muted ? 'off' : 'on'}`, act: () => { muted = !muted; } },\n    { label: () => 'Back to the game', act: () => toggleMenu() },\n  ],\n};\nfunction toggleMenu() { menu.open = !menu.open; menu.at = 0; keys.clear(); }\nfunction menuKey(key) {\n  if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'w') menu.at = (menu.at + menu.items.length - 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 's') menu.at = (menu.at + 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'Enter' || key === ' ') menu.items[menu.at].act();\n}\n\n/** The local stick: keys, the first gamepad, or a held pointer. Still while the menu is open. */\nfunction stick(me) {\n  if (menu.open) return { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };\n  let x = 0, y = 0;\n  if (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a')) x -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d')) x += 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w')) y -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s')) y += 1;\n\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\n\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"4b40bd61-d5dd-4619-9e4f-ea6c6da512d6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:19.555Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\n\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n  pad = navigator.getGamepads ? [...navigator.getGamepads()].find((p) => p && p.connected) || null : null;\n  padWas = padNow;\n  padNow = pad ? pad.buttons.map((b) => b.pressed) : [];\n  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n  if (pressed(PAD.options) && !padNow[PAD.create]) return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) {\n    if (pressed(PAD.up)) menuKey('ArrowUp');\n    if (pressed(PAD.down)) menuKey('ArrowDown');\n    if (pressed(PAD.cross)) menuKey('Enter');\n    if (pressed(PAD.circle)) toggleMenu();\n  } else if (padNow.some((b, i) => b && !padWas[i] && i !== PAD.create && i !== PAD.options)) gesture();\n}\nconst pressed = (b) => !!padNow[b] && !padWas[b];\n\n// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\nlet muted = false;\nconst menu = {\n  open: false,\n  at: 0,\n  items: [\n    { label: () => `Sound: ${muted ? 'off' : 'on'}`, act: () => { muted = !muted; } },\n    { label: () => 'Back to the game', act: () => toggleMenu() },\n  ],\n};\nfunction toggleMenu() { menu.open = !menu.open; menu.at = 0; keys.clear(); }\nfunction menuKey(key) {\n  if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'w') menu.at = (menu.at + menu.items.length - 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 's') menu.at = (menu.at + 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'Enter' || key === ' ') menu.items[menu.at].act();\n}\n\n/** The local stick: keys, the first gamepad, or a held pointer. Still while the menu is open. */\nfunction stick(me) {\n  if (menu.open) return { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };\n  let x = 0, y = 0;\n  if (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a')) x -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d')) x += 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w')) y -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s')) y += 1;\n\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\n\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016XC1HUkHos1xUBAPJiL7wx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MbnFa4xytbyeA31fKSgqtz","type":"tool_result","content":"  const all = new Set(allIds);\n  const seen = new Set();\n  const groups = [];\n  for (const group of standings) {\n    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\n    const kept = [];\n    for (const id of ids) {\n      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\n      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\n      seen.add(id);\n      kept.push(id);\n    }\n    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\n  }\n  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\n  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\n  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\n}\n\n/**\n * @param {object} o\n * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\n * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\n * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\n * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\n *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\n *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\n * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\n * @param {number} o.seed\n * @param {number} o.limitMs\n * @param {{now:()=>number, setTimeout:Function, clearTimeout:Function}} [o.clock]\n * @param {(key:string, msg:object) => void} o.deliver\n * @param {(status:object) => void} [o.onStatus]\n * @param {(record:object) => void} [o.onEnd]\n * @param {boolean} [o.gate]          the hub shows a splash and collects the players' ready itself:\n *                                    games ready up once loaded, and the round starts on release()\n */\nexport function createRound({\n  round,\n  players,\n  hostKey,\n  mode = null,\n  seed,\n  limitMs,\n  clock = REAL_CLOCK,\n  deliver,\n  onStatus = () => {},\n  onEnd = () => {},\n  timings = TIMINGS,\n  gate = false,\n  serverKey = null,\n}) {\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\n  const seats = [...players]\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\n    .map((p, id) => ({\n      id,\n      key: p.key,\n      slot: p.slot,\n      name: p.name,\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\n      hello: false,\n      ready: false,\n      out: null,\n      result: null,\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\n      progress: null,\n      stats: null,\n      awards: [],\n      caps: null,\n      hidden: null,\n    }));\n  const server = serverKey\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\n    : null;\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\n  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\n  const timers = new Set();\n  const issues = [];\n  let phase = 'loading';\n  let goAt = null;\n  let record = null;\n  let released = !gate;\n\n  const later = (ms, fn) => {\n    const handle = clock.setTimeout(() => {\n      timers.delete(handle);\n      fn();\n    }, Math.max(0, ms));\n    timers.add(handle);\n    return handle;\n  };\n  const cancel = (handle) => {\n    if (handle == null) return;\n    clock.clearTimeout(handle);\n    timers.delete(handle);\n  };\n\n  /** The players still in the round. */\n  const present = () => seats.filter((s) => !s.out);\n  /** The copies still in the round: the players, and the server. */\n  const presentCopies = () => copies.filter((s) => !s.out);\n  const selfReported = () => SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\n  const needsHost = () => !selfReported();\n  const send = (seat, msg) => deliver(seat.key, { round, ...msg });\n  const toPresent = (msg, except = null) => {\n    for (const s of presentCopies()) if (s !== except && s.hello) send(s, msg);\n  };\n  const issue = (seat, problem) => {\n    issues.push({ key: seat?.key ?? null, id: seat?.id ?? null, problem });\n    status();\n  };\n\n  function status() {\n    onStatus({\n      round,\n      phase,\n      mode,\n      host: host.id,\n      goAt,\n      gate,\n      released,\n      players: seats.map((s) => ({\n        id: s.id,\n        key: s.key,\n        slot: s.slot,\n        name: s.name,\n        color: s.color,\n        hello: s.hello,\n        ready: s.ready,\n        out: s.out,\n        result: s.result,\n        client: s.caps?.client ?? null,\n      })),\n      server: server && { id: server.id, key: server.key, hello: server.hello, ready: server.ready, out: server.out, client: server.caps?.client ?? null },\n      issues: issues.slice(),\n    });\n  }\n\n  function welcome(seat) {\n    send(seat, {\n      type: 'welcome',\n      me: seat.id,\n      host: host.id,\n      players: seats.map((s) => ({ id: s.id, name: s.name, color: s.color })),\n      keys: copies.map((s) => s.key),\n      mode,\n      seed: seed >>> 0,\n      limitMs,\n      ...(gate ? { splash: true } : {}),\n      ...(seat === server ? { server: true } : {}),\n    });\n    for (const s of seats) if (s.out) send(seat, { type: 'leave', id: s.id, reason: s.out });\n  }\n\n  function markOut(seat, reason) {\n    if (seat.out || phase === 'ended') return;\n    seat.out = reason;\n    cancel(seat.hidden);\n    seat.hidden = null;\n    toPresent({