{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015mnC2vgfCooVfCYHe4kzxy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN: a first-person open-world mercenary game inspired by Far Cry 2\n2\t\n3\t## 0. How to use this plan\n4\t\n5\t- You build the whole game from this plan and your TASK.md, alone. Nobody is available to answer questions: decide and move on. **If this plan and TASK.md disagree, TASK.md wins.**\n6\t- **Title:** yours to pick, by the rule in your TASK.md. Do that first. Nothing here depends on it. `src/data/meta.js` exports `TITLE` and `TAGLINE`, and every screen and tag reads them.\n7\t- **Names:** your TASK.md gives the dev folder's name, the deliverable HTML's name and the exit-interview file's name, so this plan never repeats them. Every path below is relative to the dev folder.\n8\t- **✔ verified** means the planner ran it on this computer on 2026-11-04 with `three@0.180.0`, `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3` and Chromium 153. Don't re-research those. Further research is optional; report whatever you do in Source Information.\n9\t- Everything in this plan is in scope. §15 lists the only things that may shrink, and they shrink in quantity, never in kind. Nothing ships half-built: if something is cut, it's absent, not stubbed.\n10\t- The \"This computer\" section of your TASK.md still applies. §14.1 lists where the planner found it needs a correction.\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## 1. The game on one page\n15\t\n16\t**Pitch.** You are a foreign mercenary in the last dry season of a dying company-state. You came for one clerk and his ledger. You stay because both sides pay on time. The grass burns where the wind takes it, your gun rusts in your hands, the fever comes back on its own schedule, and the friend who dragged you out of the fire yesterday may need you to end it for them tomorrow.\n17\t\n18\t| Decision | Choice | Why |\n19\t|---|---|---|\n20\t| Genre | Open-world first-person shooter with stealth, survival friction and a branching contract story | That is what makes the source distinct: a place that pushes back |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"7eded36f-c4ae-44ed-8c48-a70705230ae5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:03:32.433Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN: a first-person open-world mercenary game inspired by Far Cry 2\n\n## 0. How to use this plan\n\n- You build the whole game from this plan and your TASK.md, alone. Nobody is available to answer questions: decide and move on. **If this plan and TASK.md disagree, TASK.md wins.**\n- **Title:** yours to pick, by the rule in your TASK.md. Do that first. Nothing here depends on it. `src/data/meta.js` exports `TITLE` and `TAGLINE`, and every screen and tag reads them.\n- **Names:** your TASK.md gives the dev folder's name, the deliverable HTML's name and the exit-interview file's name, so this plan never repeats them. Every path below is relative to the dev folder.\n- **✔ verified** means the planner ran it on this computer on 2026-11-04 with `three@0.180.0`, `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3` and Chromium 153. Don't re-research those. Further research is optional; report whatever you do in Source Information.\n- Everything in this plan is in scope. §15 lists the only things that may shrink, and they shrink in quantity, never in kind. Nothing ships half-built: if something is cut, it's absent, not stubbed.\n- The \"This computer\" section of your TASK.md still applies. §14.1 lists where the planner found it needs a correction.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game on one page\n\n**Pitch.** You are a foreign mercenary in the last dry season of a dying company-state. You came for one clerk and his ledger. You stay because both sides pay on time. The grass burns where the wind takes it, your gun rusts in your hands, the fever comes back on its own schedule, and the friend who dragged you out of the fire yesterday may need you to end it for them tomorrow.\n\n| Decision | Choice | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Genre | Open-world first-person shooter with stealth, survival friction and a branching contract story | That is what makes the source distinct: a place that pushes back |","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1160}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015mnC2vgfCooVfCYHe4kzxy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
