{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCLhgYdmShVDhtri4Jf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LYUCSxQZzP58BqGRFd8Y6a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old,new,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, ('MISSING: '+old[:80])\n    s=s.replace(old,new) if count==0 else s.replace(old,new,count)\n\n# A. Title\nrep(\"- **Title:** yours to pick, by the rule in your TASK.md. Do that first. Nothing here depends on it.\",\n    \"- **Title:** yours to pick, by the rule in your TASK.md (a riff, never the source's actual name). Do that first. Nothing here depends on it.\")\n\n# B. Map table\nrep(\"| `landing` | **The Landing** | −55, 232 | Barge jetty on the Marrow. Prologue ends here |\",\n    \"| `landing` | **The Landing** | −55, 212 | Barge jetty on the Marrow. Prologue ends here |\")\nrep(\"| `bridge_road` | **Kiln Bridge** | 120, 60 | Old road bridge east across the Marrow into the Long Grass |\",\n    \"| `bridge_road` | **Kiln Bridge** | 130, 60 | Old road bridge east across the Marrow, the only road to the east bank. South-east to the Long Grass, north-east to the Workings |\")\nrep(\"| `s3` | Safehouse **Signal Box** | 120, −395 | On the rail line. Must be taken |\",\n    \"| `s3` | Safehouse **Signal Box** | 120, −395 | On the rail line. Optional: clear its guards and it's yours (Salt Shed is the same, through C4) |\")\nrep(\"| `gp5` | Post **Workings Gate** | 480, −520 | Stewards at start |\",\n    \"| `gp5` | Post **Workings Gate** | 570, −370 | East bank, where the road and rail meet the pit's fence. Stewards at start |\")\nrep(\"| `gp7` | Post **Low Ford** | −500, 390 | Vehicle ford toward the camp. Commons at start |\",\n    \"| `gp7` | Post **Low Ford** | −500, 390 | Vehicle ford toward the camp. Commons at start |\\n| `gp8` | Post **North Road** | 380, −60 | East bank, on the road from Kiln Bridge to the Workings. Stewards at start |\")\nrep(\"| `workings` | **The Workings** | 640, −640 | Terraced open pit, about 180 m radius, 40 m deep. Conveyor, sheds, strongroom at the bottom |\",\n    \"| `workings` | **The Workings** | 760, −430 | East bank. Terraced open pit, about 180 m radius, 40 m deep. Conveyor, sheds, strongroom at the bottom |\")\nrep(\"- **The Marrow:** a spline through (900, −1024), (860, −700), (600, −420), (330, −330), (180, −60), (60, 180), (−120, 290), (−420, 360), (−760, 470), (−1024, 720). Carved 6 m deep, 30–60 m wide.\",\n    \"- **The Marrow:** a spline through (900, −1024), (760, −740), (540, −560), (470, −380), (400, −220), (200, −60), (60, 180), (−120, 290), (−420, 360), (−760, 470), (−1024, 720). Carved 6 m deep, 30–60 m wide. It splits the map: Kiln, the Depot and the Escarpment on the west bank; the Long Grass, the Dump, the Workings and Second Water on the east and south.\")\nrep(\"- **Rail line:** from `depot` along z ≈ −380 to `railbridge`, then to `workings`.\",\n    \"- **Rail line:** from `depot` along z ≈ −380, past Signal Box, over `railbridge`, to the pit's west side.\\n- **Roads:** Kiln north gate → Junction → Rail Crossing → Depot Road → Switchback Foot → Mission. Kiln east gate → Yard → Kiln Bridge, then forking to Grass Road → Dump and to North Road → Workings Gate. A west road from Kiln to Low Ford → Second Water.\")\n\n# D. AI archetypes and patrols\nrep(\"- **Death:** hit reaction → ragdoll (§11).\",\n    \"- **Archetypes:** guard, sergeant (150 hp, calls flanks), gunner (mounted guns and Belt Gun), fire team (Drip Torch, lights grass on purpose, late game and The Job).\\n- **Patrol trucks:** 2–3 per faction on road splines. Chase when alerted, with a gunner firing, and stop 30 m out to dismount. Papers apply to them too (a wave, a slow-down, or a fight).\\n- **Death:** hit reaction → ragdoll (§11).\")\n\n# E. Ceasefire\nrep(\"- **Kiln ceasefire.** Weapons holster at the gates. Fire a shot in town and both sides' gate guards turn hostile for a game day, the fixers refuse you, and the Widow charges +1.\",\n    \"- **Kiln ceasefire** (Second Water too). Weapons holster at the gates, and drawing takes a deliberate long press. Fire a shot in town and both sides' gate guards turn hostile for a game day, the fixers refuse you, and the Widow charges +1.\")\n\n# F. Map focus while driving\nrep(\"Circle or Esc lowers it. Big text only, no pins legend.\",\n    \"Circle or Esc lowers it. Big text only, no pins legend. At the wheel, focusing takes your hands off: the truck coasts and brakes gently until you lower it.\")\n\n# G. Twist substitution\nrep(\"- **Twist.** After you accept a contract, the highest-trust suitable buddy radios or meets you with a better, riskier way: an extra objective, more pay, +10 trust. They show up on site and fight alongside you.\",\n    \"- **Twist.** After you accept a contract, a buddy radios or meets you with a better, riskier way: an extra objective, more pay, +10 trust. They show up on site and fight alongside you. Each twist names a default merc. If that merc is you, or dead, the next living buddy by trust takes the same lines, so write them to fit anyone. No buddies left: no twists, no rescues, and the game still completes.\")\n\n# H. Contract failure\nrep(\"Each step type is a small handler. Documented in `docs/DESIGNER.md`, validated by `tools/validate-data.mjs`.\",\n    \"Each step type is a small handler. Documented in `docs/DESIGNER.md`, validated by `tools/validate-data.mjs`.\\n\\n**Nothing dead-ends.** A failed contract (dynamite truck lost, target escaped) is re-offered after the next sleep at lower pay, with any lost vehicle or item re-issued. A contract that needs a destroyed thing to still exist re-checks world state first and adjusts. The bot playthrough tests one failure and retry.\")\n\n# I. C2 and C6 routes, C3 consequence\nrep(\"- *Beats:* drive out (bluff `gp3` if you came that way, go through or around `gp2`), climb the rise,\",\n    \"- *Beats:* drive out over Kiln Bridge (through or around `gp2`), climb the rise,\")\nrep(\"The camp's rail road is gone (`camp.count` −20, or +15 if you'd delivered E1 first: people left in time).\",\n    \"The rail was the camp's way out (`camp.count` −20, or +15 if you'd delivered E1 first: people left in time).\")\nrep(\"Bumps damage cargo, fire detonates it. The papers scene at `gp3` is at its tensest here. A sticky-handed sergeant might search you.\",\n    \"Bumps damage cargo, fire detonates it. The papers scene at `gp8` is at its tensest here: a sticky-handed sergeant might search you. `gp5` is next.\")\n\n# J. The Job details\nrep(\"All start at Salt Jetty (river's east bank near Kiln Bridge) with two pickups.\",\n    \"All start at Salt Jetty (150, 110, on the east bank just below Kiln Bridge) with two pickups.\")\nrep(\"With only one player in a round, one AI buddy (Ines) comes along, run by the host.\",\n    \"With only one player in a round, one AI buddy (the next merc in seat order) comes along, run by the host.\")\n\n# K. Always send\nrep(\"- Coalesce into one outbox per tick. `send()` returning `false` is a test failure.\",\n    \"- Coalesce into one outbox per tick. `send()` returning `false` is a test failure. Keep sending `me` and `s` from `start` even when nothing changed, including on a server copy (the harness checks traffic flows both ways on every copy).\")\n\n# L. Pad disconnect, loading\nrep(\"- **Prompts follow the last input used.**\",\n    \"- **Boot:** a DOM loading screen with `TITLE` appears within the first moment, before any heavy work. Yield between world-build stages. Keys pressed during load are harmless.\\n- **Pad unplugged in play:** auto-pause with one big line and a resume prompt. A pad or key press carries on.\\n- **Prompts follow the last input used.**\")\n\n# M. Attract reel\na=s.index(\"| # | Vignette | Shows |\")\nb=s.index(\"No sound until the browser has had a gesture\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"| # | Vignette | Shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Kiln at morning: walk the market, gun holstered, the Widow's table, a buy, a fresh gun from the crate | `ceasefire_town`, `shop_buy`, `armoury_redraw` |\n| 2 | Pickup at golden hour on the Grass Road, map up, focus to set a waypoint, GPS arrow | `drive`, `map_raise`, `map_focus`, `map_drive`, `gps_waypoint`, `day_night` |\n| 3 | Checkpoint: papers out the window, waved on. Next post: \"Out of the truck.\" | `papers_ok`, `papers_fail` |\n| 4 | Ridge at dusk: monocular, tag guards, flare into grass, front sweeps a post, herd bolts, tanks blow | `monocular_tag`, `flare_ignite`, `fire_spread`, `animals_flee`, `explosion_physics` |\n| 5 | Firefight at Junction: a rusty gun jams, clears, then comes apart. Grab a looted carbine. Ragdolls, a man crawling, a comrade dragging him, post falls quiet | `rust_visual`, `jam`, `jam_clear`, `gun_break`, `loot_gun`, `ragdoll`, `wounded_crawl`, `comrade_drag`, `post_clear` |\n| 6 | All four surgeries in cover, then a syringe | `surgery_bullet`, `surgery_finger`, `surgery_shrapnel`, `surgery_burn`, `heal_syringe` |\n| 7 | Fever on the road: world warps, bottle, dose, recovery | `fever`, `pill` |\n| 8 | Down in the dirt, buddy runs in, drag, pistol in hand. Then the buddy goes down: morphine | `rescue`, `buddy_down`, `mercy` |\n| 9 | Ferry to Bridge Pier, skiff to the capsized barge, locator hunt, a case, a tape | `ferry`, `skiff`, `locator_found`, `diamond`, `dictation` |\n| 10 | Engine hit, hood up, wrench under fire. Then a Technical on the mounted gun | `breakdown`, `repair`, `mounted_gun` |\n| 11 | Night sneak through tall grass past lamp guards: machete, then a Molotov | `night_stealth`, `crouch_grass`, `machete_takedown`, `molotov` |\n| 12 | Bed and watch, hands spin, light sweeps the shutters | `sleep_time` |\n| 13 | The Tube at a truck, then the bridge goes with the train on it, chase-cam fly-by | `rocket`, `train`, `explosion_physics` |\n| 14 | Wind turns, Drip Torch, wall of fire, trees burn, embers jump the road, title card | `torch_flame`, `wind_shift`, `tree_burn`, `ember_spot` |\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nrep(\"- **Each vignette** states up to a few things it wants shown, so the reel is mostly genuine AI play: the bot moves, shoots, heals. About 25–35 s each, 5 minutes a loop:\",\n    \"- **It runs in its own throwaway sim**, never touching the player's save or settings. Exit discards it and returns to the title scene.\\n- **Each vignette** states up to a few things it wants shown, so the reel is mostly genuine AI play: the bot moves, shoots, heals. About 25–35 s each, 6–7 minutes a loop. Together they cover at least 80% of the F-list:\")\n\n# N. Layout\nrep(\"tools/            build.mjs, test.mjs, tests/*, hub/ (harness.html, bridge.js, round.js), balance.mjs, validate-data.mjs\",\n    \"tools/            build.mjs, test.mjs, tests/*, hub/ (harness.html, bridge.js, round.js), balance.mjs, validate-data.mjs, shots.mjs\")\n\n# O. Recipes: grass and smoke\nrep(\"\"\"const toBurnUV = (xz) => xz.div(2048).add(0.5);\nconst off = attribute('instOffset', 'vec3');           // InstancedBufferGeometry attribute\n\"\"\",\"\"\"// Geometry: a thin ConeGeometry tuft (translate up by half its height, set every normal to 0,1,0), wrapped in an\n// InstancedBufferGeometry: copy index, position, normal and uv; setAttribute('instOffset', new\n// THREE.InstancedBufferAttribute(offsets, 3)); set instanceCount; mesh.frustumCulled = false.\n// windDir = uniform(new THREE.Vector2(1, 0.3)), windStr = uniform(0.5). burnTex rows run with z, as the fire grid does.\nconst toBurnUV = (xz) => xz.div(2048).add(0.5);\nconst off = attribute('instOffset', 'vec3');\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"const inst = attribute('fireInst', 'vec4');            // xyz position, w size\n\"\"\",\"\"\"// Geometry: PlaneGeometry(1, 1) translated up by 0.5, wrapped in an InstancedBufferGeometry as above.\nconst inst = attribute('fireInst', 'vec4');            // xyz position, w size\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"fireMat.fog = false;\n```\n\nPool about 3000 flame cards on the nearest burning cells, about 600 smoke cards in rising columns (rounded, two-tone, ink-outlined), and embers.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"fireMat.fog = false;\n// Smoke: the same card with the same billboard (w grows with height, stacked in rising columns):\nconst puff = Fn(() => {\n  const seed = inst.x.mul(0.7).add(inst.y.mul(0.4));\n  const n = mx_noise_float(vec3(vuv.mul(2.6).add(seed), time.mul(0.15))).mul(0.5).add(0.5);\n  return float(1).sub(length(vuv.sub(vec2(0.5, 0.5))).mul(2)).add(n.mul(0.45).sub(0.12));\n})();\nsmokeMat.opacityNode = puff; smokeMat.alphaTestNode = float(0.12);\nsmokeMat.colorNode = mix(color(0x2a2522), color(0x5b4d43), step(0.42, puff));\n```\n\nPool about 3000 flame cards on the nearest burning cells, about 600 smoke cards in rising columns (rounded, two-tone, ink-outlined), and embers.\"\"\")\n\n# P. Vehicle axes\nrep(\"\"\"const veh = world.createVehicleController(chassis);\nfor (const w of\"\"\",\"\"\"const veh = world.createVehicleController(chassis);\nveh.indexUpAxis = 1; veh.setIndexForwardAxis = 2;      // yes, that one is a setter named setIndexForwardAxis\nfor (const w of\"\"\")\nrep(\"// Raycast vehicle: forward is +z, ✔ 2500 N on rear wheels reaches about 16 m/s in 5 s\",\n    \"// Raycast vehicle: set forward to +z as below. ✔ 2500 N on each rear wheel reaches about 16 m/s in 5 s\")\n\n# Q. Playthrough, hub matrix, folder\nrep(\"- **Scripted whole-game playthrough (`sim/bot.js`):** a bot playing through **input frames only** (god mode allowed, no state edits) from the barge through every contract, twists on, to each of the three endings (re-loading the save before the choice). Assert world-state consequences at each step, and **F-list coverage 100%**. Also a shorter run of The Job with bots in four seats.\",\n    \"- **Scripted whole-game playthrough (`sim/bot.js`):** a bot playing through **input frames only** from the barge through every contract, twists on, to each of the three endings (re-loading the save before the choice). God mode and the dev Trigger commands are allowed, to force rare events on schedule. No other state edits. Assert world-state consequences at each step. Also a shorter run of The Job with bots in four seats. **Together these must reach F-list coverage of 100%.**\")\na=s.index(\"harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\")\nb=s.index(\"Then:\\n\\n- **The game on its own**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=server&play=8000\n```\n\nRun these with the flags from §14.1, and the 4-player case once more with no flags: that is the hub's default browser, where every copy is on WebGL2 in software. Give each page up to 300 s, as the hub does. HARNESS_CLAIM\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nrep(\"- Run one browser at a time. A 4-copy harness run is one browser but heavy.\",\n    \"- Everything you make stays in your dev folder, and you read nothing outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside yours.\\n- Run one browser at a time. A 4-copy harness run is one browser but heavy.\")\n\n# R. Scale knobs\nrep(\"| Posts | 7 | 4 |\",\"| Posts | 8 | 4 |\")\nrep(\"| Attract vignettes | 12 | 8 (≥ 80% of what remains of the F-list) |\",\"| Attract vignettes | 14 | 10 (≥ 80% of what remains of the F-list) |\")\n\n# S. Target image words\nrep(\"advancing over a sea of pale gold grass with a black burnt scar behind,\",\"advancing over a sea of gold grass with a black burnt scar behind,\")\n\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"HARNESS_CLAIM\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-200; wc -w PLAN.md","description":"Apply review fixes to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2239,"cache_read_input_tokens":342459,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2239},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"fe6e9f02-a540-44e7-a7e9-865934a96dbf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:38.468Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCLhPBNwPnZEhw3ZLv2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LYUCSxQZzP58BqGRFd8Y6a":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old,new,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, ('MISSING: '+old[:80])\n    s=s.replace(old,new) if count==0 else s.replace(old,new,count)\n\n# A. Title\nrep(\"- **Title:** yours to pick, by the rule in your TASK.md. Do that first. Nothing here depends on it.\",\n    \"- **Title:** yours to pick, by the rule in your TASK.md (a riff, never the source's actual name). Do that first. Nothing here depends on it.\")\n\n# B. Map table\nrep(\"| `landing` | **The Landing** | −55, 232 | Barge jetty on the Marrow. Prologue ends here |\",\n    \"| `landing` | **The Landing** | −55, 212 | Barge jetty on the Marrow. Prologue ends here |\")\nrep(\"| `bridge_road` | **Kiln Bridge** | 120, 60 | Old road bridge east across the Marrow into the Long Grass |\",\n    \"| `bridge_road` | **Kiln Bridge** | 130, 60 | Old road bridge east across the Marrow, the only road to the east bank. South-east to the Long Grass, north-east to the Workings |\")\nrep(\"| `s3` | Safehouse **Signal Box** | 120, −395 | On the rail line. Must be taken |\",\n    \"| `s3` | Safehouse **Signal Box** | 120, −395 | On the rail line. Optional: clear its guards and it's yours (Salt Shed is the same, through C4) |\")\nrep(\"| `gp5` | Post **Workings Gate** | 480, −520 | Stewards at start |\",\n    \"| `gp5` | Post **Workings Gate** | 570, −370 | East bank, where the road and rail meet the pit's fence. Stewards at start |\")\nrep(\"| `gp7` | Post **Low Ford** | −500, 390 | Vehicle ford toward the camp. Commons at start |\",\n    \"| `gp7` | Post **Low Ford** | −500, 390 | Vehicle ford toward the camp. Commons at start |\\n| `gp8` | Post **North Road** | 380, −60 | East bank, on the road from Kiln Bridge to the Workings. Stewards at start |\")\nrep(\"| `workings` | **The Workings** | 640, −640 | Terraced open pit, about 180 m radius, 40 m deep. Conveyor, sheds, strongroom at the bottom |\",\n    \"| `workings` | **The Workings** | 760, −430 | East bank. Terraced open pit, about 180 m radius, 40 m deep. Conveyor, sheds, strongroom at the bottom |\")\nrep(\"- **The Marrow:** a spline through (900, −1024), (860, −700), (600, −420), (330, −330), (180, −60), (60, 180), (−120, 290), (−420, 360), (−760, 470), (−1024, 720). Carved 6 m deep, 30–60 m wide.\",\n    \"- **The Marrow:** a spline through (900, −1024), (760, −740), (540, −560), (470, −380), (400, −220), (200, −60), (60, 180), (−120, 290), (−420, 360), (−760, 470), (−1024, 720). Carved 6 m deep, 30–60 m wide. It splits the map: Kiln, the Depot and the Escarpment on the west bank; the Long Grass, the Dump, the Workings and Second Water on the east and south.\")\nrep(\"- **Rail line:** from `depot` along z ≈ −380 to `railbridge`, then to `workings`.\",\n    \"- **Rail line:** from `depot` along z ≈ −380, past Signal Box, over `railbridge`, to the pit's west side.\\n- **Roads:** Kiln north gate → Junction → Rail Crossing → Depot Road → Switchback Foot → Mission. Kiln east gate → Yard → Kiln Bridge, then forking to Grass Road → Dump and to North Road → Workings Gate. A west road from Kiln to Low Ford → Second Water.\")\n\n# D. AI archetypes and patrols\nrep(\"- **Death:** hit reaction → ragdoll (§11).\",\n    \"- **Archetypes:** guard, sergeant (150 hp, calls flanks), gunner (mounted guns and Belt Gun), fire team (Drip Torch, lights grass on purpose, late game and The Job).\\n- **Patrol trucks:** 2–3 per faction on road splines. Chase when alerted, with a gunner firing, and stop 30 m out to dismount. Papers apply to them too (a wave, a slow-down, or a fight).\\n- **Death:** hit reaction → ragdoll (§11).\")\n\n# E. Ceasefire\nrep(\"- **Kiln ceasefire.** Weapons holster at the gates. Fire a shot in town and both sides' gate guards turn hostile for a game day, the fixers refuse you, and the Widow charges +1.\",\n    \"- **Kiln ceasefire** (Second Water too). Weapons holster at the gates, and drawing takes a deliberate long press. Fire a shot in town and both sides' gate guards turn hostile for a game day, the fixers refuse you, and the Widow charges +1.\")\n\n# F. Map focus while driving\nrep(\"Circle or Esc lowers it. Big text only, no pins legend.\",\n    \"Circle or Esc lowers it. Big text only, no pins legend. At the wheel, focusing takes your hands off: the truck coasts and brakes gently until you lower it.\")\n\n# G. Twist substitution\nrep(\"- **Twist.** After you accept a contract, the highest-trust suitable buddy radios or meets you with a better, riskier way: an extra objective, more pay, +10 trust. They show up on site and fight alongside you.\",\n    \"- **Twist.** After you accept a contract, a buddy radios or meets you with a better, riskier way: an extra objective, more pay, +10 trust. They show up on site and fight alongside you. Each twist names a default merc. If that merc is you, or dead, the next living buddy by trust takes the same lines, so write them to fit anyone. No buddies left: no twists, no rescues, and the game still completes.\")\n\n# H. Contract failure\nrep(\"Each step type is a small handler. Documented in `docs/DESIGNER.md`, validated by `tools/validate-data.mjs`.\",\n    \"Each step type is a small handler. Documented in `docs/DESIGNER.md`, validated by `tools/validate-data.mjs`.\\n\\n**Nothing dead-ends.** A failed contract (dynamite truck lost, target escaped) is re-offered after the next sleep at lower pay, with any lost vehicle or item re-issued. A contract that needs a destroyed thing to still exist re-checks world state first and adjusts. The bot playthrough tests one failure and retry.\")\n\n# I. C2 and C6 routes, C3 consequence\nrep(\"- *Beats:* drive out (bluff `gp3` if you came that way, go through or around `gp2`), climb the rise,\",\n    \"- *Beats:* drive out over Kiln Bridge (through or around `gp2`), climb the rise,\")\nrep(\"The camp's rail road is gone (`camp.count` −20, or +15 if you'd delivered E1 first: people left in time).\",\n    \"The rail was the camp's way out (`camp.count` −20, or +15 if you'd delivered E1 first: people left in time).\")\nrep(\"Bumps damage cargo, fire detonates it. The papers scene at `gp3` is at its tensest here. A sticky-handed sergeant might search you.\",\n    \"Bumps damage cargo, fire detonates it. The papers scene at `gp8` is at its tensest here: a sticky-handed sergeant might search you. `gp5` is next.\")\n\n# J. The Job details\nrep(\"All start at Salt Jetty (river's east bank near Kiln Bridge) with two pickups.\",\n    \"All start at Salt Jetty (150, 110, on the east bank just below Kiln Bridge) with two pickups.\")\nrep(\"With only one player in a round, one AI buddy (Ines) comes along, run by the host.\",\n    \"With only one player in a round, one AI buddy (the next merc in seat order) comes along, run by the host.\")\n\n# K. Always send\nrep(\"- Coalesce into one outbox per tick. `send()` returning `false` is a test failure.\",\n    \"- Coalesce into one outbox per tick. `send()` returning `false` is a test failure. Keep sending `me` and `s` from `start` even when nothing changed, including on a server copy (the harness checks traffic flows both ways on every copy).\")\n\n# L. Pad disconnect, loading\nrep(\"- **Prompts follow the last input used.**\",\n    \"- **Boot:** a DOM loading screen with `TITLE` appears within the first moment, before any heavy work. Yield between world-build stages. Keys pressed during load are harmless.\\n- **Pad unplugged in play:** auto-pause with one big line and a resume prompt. A pad or key press carries on.\\n- **Prompts follow the last input used.**\")\n\n# M. Attract reel\na=s.index(\"| # | Vignette | Shows |\")\nb=s.index(\"No sound until the browser has had a gesture\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"| # | Vignette | Shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Kiln at morning: walk the market, gun holstered, the Widow's table, a buy, a fresh gun from the crate | `ceasefire_town`, `shop_buy`, `armoury_redraw` |\n| 2 | Pickup at golden hour on the Grass Road, map up, focus to set a waypoint, GPS arrow | `drive`, `map_raise`, `map_focus`, `map_drive`, `gps_waypoint`, `day_night` |\n| 3 | Checkpoint: papers out the window, waved on. Next post: \"Out of the truck.\" | `papers_ok`, `papers_fail` |\n| 4 | Ridge at dusk: monocular, tag guards, flare into grass, front sweeps a post, herd bolts, tanks blow | `monocular_tag`, `flare_ignite`, `fire_spread`, `animals_flee`, `explosion_physics` |\n| 5 | Firefight at Junction: a rusty gun jams, clears, then comes apart. Grab a looted carbine. Ragdolls, a man crawling, a comrade dragging him, post falls quiet | `rust_visual`, `jam`, `jam_clear`, `gun_break`, `loot_gun`, `ragdoll`, `wounded_crawl`, `comrade_drag`, `post_clear` |\n| 6 | All four surgeries in cover, then a syringe | `surgery_bullet`, `surgery_finger`, `surgery_shrapnel`, `surgery_burn`, `heal_syringe` |\n| 7 | Fever on the road: world warps, bottle, dose, recovery | `fever`, `pill` |\n| 8 | Down in the dirt, buddy runs in, drag, pistol in hand. Then the buddy goes down: morphine | `rescue`, `buddy_down`, `mercy` |\n| 9 | Ferry to Bridge Pier, skiff to the capsized barge, locator hunt, a case, a tape | `ferry`, `skiff`, `locator_found`, `diamond`, `dictation` |\n| 10 | Engine hit, hood up, wrench under fire. Then a Technical on the mounted gun | `breakdown`, `repair`, `mounted_gun` |\n| 11 | Night sneak through tall grass past lamp guards: machete, then a Molotov | `night_stealth`, `crouch_grass`, `machete_takedown`, `molotov` |\n| 12 | Bed and watch, hands spin, light sweeps the shutters | `sleep_time` |\n| 13 | The Tube at a truck, then the bridge goes with the train on it, chase-cam fly-by | `rocket`, `train`, `explosion_physics` |\n| 14 | Wind turns, Drip Torch, wall of fire, trees burn, embers jump the road, title card | `torch_flame`, `wind_shift`, `tree_burn`, `ember_spot` |\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nrep(\"- **Each vignette** states up to a few things it wants shown, so the reel is mostly genuine AI play: the bot moves, shoots, heals. About 25–35 s each, 5 minutes a loop:\",\n    \"- **It runs in its own throwaway sim**, never touching the player's save or settings. Exit discards it and returns to the title scene.\\n- **Each vignette** states up to a few things it wants shown, so the reel is mostly genuine AI play: the bot moves, shoots, heals. About 25–35 s each, 6–7 minutes a loop. Together they cover at least 80% of the F-list:\")\n\n# N. Layout\nrep(\"tools/            build.mjs, test.mjs, tests/*, hub/ (harness.html, bridge.js, round.js), balance.mjs, validate-data.mjs\",\n    \"tools/            build.mjs, test.mjs, tests/*, hub/ (harness.html, bridge.js, round.js), balance.mjs, validate-data.mjs, shots.mjs\")\n\n# O. Recipes: grass and smoke\nrep(\"\"\"const toBurnUV = (xz) => xz.div(2048).add(0.5);\nconst off = attribute('instOffset', 'vec3');           // InstancedBufferGeometry attribute\n\"\"\",\"\"\"// Geometry: a thin ConeGeometry tuft (translate up by half its height, set every normal to 0,1,0), wrapped in an\n// InstancedBufferGeometry: copy index, position, normal and uv; setAttribute('instOffset', new\n// THREE.InstancedBufferAttribute(offsets, 3)); set instanceCount; mesh.frustumCulled = false.\n// windDir = uniform(new THREE.Vector2(1, 0.3)), windStr = uniform(0.5). burnTex rows run with z, as the fire grid does.\nconst toBurnUV = (xz) => xz.div(2048).add(0.5);\nconst off = attribute('instOffset', 'vec3');\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"const inst = attribute('fireInst', 'vec4');            // xyz position, w size\n\"\"\",\"\"\"// Geometry: PlaneGeometry(1, 1) translated up by 0.5, wrapped in an InstancedBufferGeometry as above.\nconst inst = attribute('fireInst', 'vec4');            // xyz position, w size\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"fireMat.fog = false;\n```\n\nPool about 3000 flame cards on the nearest burning cells, about 600 smoke cards in rising columns (rounded, two-tone, ink-outlined), and embers.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"fireMat.fog = false;\n// Smoke: the same card with the same billboard (w grows with height, stacked in rising columns):\nconst puff = Fn(() => {\n  const seed = inst.x.mul(0.7).add(inst.y.mul(0.4));\n  const n = mx_noise_float(vec3(vuv.mul(2.6).add(seed), time.mul(0.15))).mul(0.5).add(0.5);\n  return float(1).sub(length(vuv.sub(vec2(0.5, 0.5))).mul(2)).add(n.mul(0.45).sub(0.12));\n})();\nsmokeMat.opacityNode = puff; smokeMat.alphaTestNode = float(0.12);\nsmokeMat.colorNode = mix(color(0x2a2522), color(0x5b4d43), step(0.42, puff));\n```\n\nPool about 3000 flame cards on the nearest burning cells, about 600 smoke cards in rising columns (rounded, two-tone, ink-outlined), and embers.\"\"\")\n\n# P. Vehicle axes\nrep(\"\"\"const veh = world.createVehicleController(chassis);\nfor (const w of\"\"\",\"\"\"const veh = world.createVehicleController(chassis);\nveh.indexUpAxis = 1; veh.setIndexForwardAxis = 2;      // yes, that one is a setter named setIndexForwardAxis\nfor (const w of\"\"\")\nrep(\"// Raycast vehicle: forward is +z, ✔ 2500 N on rear wheels reaches about 16 m/s in 5 s\",\n    \"// Raycast vehicle: set forward to +z as below. ✔ 2500 N on each rear wheel reaches about 16 m/s in 5 s\")\n\n# Q. Playthrough, hub matrix, folder\nrep(\"- **Scripted whole-game playthrough (`sim/bot.js`):** a bot playing through **input frames only** (god mode allowed, no state edits) from the barge through every contract, twists on, to each of the three endings (re-loading the save before the choice). Assert world-state consequences at each step, and **F-list coverage 100%**. Also a shorter run of The Job with bots in four seats.\",\n    \"- **Scripted whole-game playthrough (`sim/bot.js`):** a bot playing through **input frames only** from the barge through every contract, twists on, to each of the three endings (re-loading the save before the choice). God mode and the dev Trigger commands are allowed, to force rare events on schedule. No other state edits. Assert world-state consequences at each step. Also a shorter run of The Job with bots in four seats. **Together these must reach F-list coverage of 100%.**\")\na=s.index(\"harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\")\nb=s.index(\"Then:\\n\\n- **The game on its own**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave&play=8000\nharness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=server&play=8000\n```\n\nRun these with the flags from §14.1, and the 4-player case once more with no flags: that is the hub's default browser, where every copy is on WebGL2 in software. Give each page up to 300 s, as the hub does. HARNESS_CLAIM\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nrep(\"- Run one browser at a time. A 4-copy harness run is one browser but heavy.\",\n    \"- Everything you make stays in your dev folder, and you read nothing outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside yours.\\n- Run one browser at a time. A 4-copy harness run is one browser but heavy.\")\n\n# R. Scale knobs\nrep(\"| Posts | 7 | 4 |\",\"| Posts | 8 | 4 |\")\nrep(\"| Attract vignettes | 12 | 8 (≥ 80% of what remains of the F-list) |\",\"| Attract vignettes | 14 | 10 (≥ 80% of what remains of the F-list) |\")\n\n# S. Target image words\nrep(\"advancing over a sea of pale gold grass with a black burnt scar behind,\",\"advancing over a sea of gold grass with a black burnt scar behind,\")\n\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"HARNESS_CLAIM\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-200; wc -w PLAN.md","description":"Apply review fixes to the plan"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01LYUCSxQZzP58BqGRFd8Y6a":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work"}}}
