{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCRqwmXyxeAJ2uvMzUx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EoQytRn1ACmqR4L86LqASs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":340},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14020,"cache_read_input_tokens":353045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14020},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"5594d6ca-277b-4827-b186-d4aa6b7dc23d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:47.673Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCRqcvXoDjGeoqFEfaN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EoQytRn1ACmqR4L86LqASs":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":340}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EoQytRn1ACmqR4L86LqASs","type":"tool_result","content":"330\t\n331\t### 4.12 Factions and world state\n332\t\n333\t`world.state` holds: post owners and garrisons; `dump` and `railbridge` status; standing with each faction (−100..100, start 0); papers; `camp.count` (starts at 212, changed by your choices and consequences); buddy states; dictations found; chosen side; flags. Contract `onComplete` actions change it. Dialogue variants and the camp's look (crowded, thinning, ash on the tents) read it. The ending ledger prints from it.\n334\t\n335\t### 4.13 Contract runner\n336\t\n337\t`src/sim/contracts.js` runs declarative data from `src/data/contracts.js`.\n338\t\n339\t```js\n340\t{ id:'c2', title:'Dry Grass', giver:'comptroller', requires:['c1'], side:'stewards', pay:6,\n341\t  offer:['line id',…], twist:{ buddy:'tomasz', line:'…', pay:3, trust:10, steps:[…] },\n342\t  steps:[ {do:'goto', poi:'dump', r:90, note:'…'}, {do:'destroy', tags:['dump_tank'], count:3},\n343\t          {do:'return', npc:'comptroller'} ],\n344\t  onComplete:[ {set:'post.gp2.owner', to:'stewards'}, {add:'standing.commons', by:-20},\n345\t               {add:'camp.count', by:-12}, {ledger:'…'} ] }\n346\t```\n347\t\n348\tStep vocabulary: `goto, talk, interact (hold), collect, destroy, kill, plant, survive, hold_zone, escort, deliver, drive_cargo, sleep_until, choice, wait_event`. Each step type is a small handler. Documented in `docs/DESIGNER.md`, validated by `tools/validate-data.mjs`.\n349\t\n350\t**Nothing dead-ends.** A failed contract (dynamite truck lost, target escaped) is re-offered after the next sleep at lower pay, with any lost vehicle or item re-issued. A contract that needs a destroyed thing to still exist re-checks world state first and adjusts. The bot playthrough tests one failure and retry.\n351\t\n352\t---\n353\t\n354\t## 5. Story and writing\n355\t\n356\t### 5.1 Voice (narrative tone)\n357\t\n358\tA weary, literate, morally exhausted voice, in the spirit of the source's Conrad-flavoured bleakness, with **our own rhetorical signature: bookkeeping**. Everyone talks about violence as accounts, shifts, invoices, rates, write-offs. Rules:\n359\t\n360\t- Short declarative sentences. People talk while doing something else, and they don't stop because you walked off.\n361\t- Nobody explains the theme. Nobody winks. Humour is dry and dead-eyed.\n362\t- No \"chosen one\". You're a line item and everyone knows it.\n363\t- Subtitles are the only real language (voices are gibberish, §12). Two lines at most, big type.\n364\t\n365\t**Samples, to set the bar. Write the rest in this voice.**\n366\t\n367\t> **Ferryman:** First time? … Everyone says it's their last. Mostly they're right.\n368\t>\n369\t> **Widow:** New barrel, no rust, no history. That's more than you can say for anyone who's ever bought one.\n370\t>\n371\t> **Comptroller:** We don't say \"war\" in this office. We say \"adverse operating conditions\". You'll burn the Commons' diesel before Thursday. Invoice me for the matches.\n372\t>\n373\t> **Foreman:** My grandfather dug that pit. My father dug it deeper. I'm the first of us who gets to fill it.\n374\t>\n375\t> **Doctor:** Nothing here cures. It only moves the bill to next week.\n376\t>\n377\t> **Clerk of Second Water:** Two hundred and twelve this morning. You can tell whoever pays you that I counted.\n378\t>\n379\t> **Ines (rescue):** Don't look at it. Look at me. There. That's the worst of it over, and I'm lying.\n380\t>\n381\t> **Tomasz (rescue):** I said I'd come back for you. I also said that to my wife. Get up.\n382\t>\n383\t> **Dao (rescue):** You owe me four diamonds and a leg. Yours, if I have to carry you again.\n384\t>\n385\t> **Sefton (rescue):** Thirty years I've been leaving this place. Up you come.\n386\t>\n387\t> **Guards:** \"Wind's coming round! Leave it, leave it!\" · \"It's stuck, it's stuck!\" · \"Don't leave me for the birds.\" · \"Got you. Stop helping.\"\n388\t\n389\tWrite at least: 4 rescue lines per buddy; 12 lines per fixer; 20 guard barks per category (spotted, lost you, fire, jam, wounded, dragging, reload, ceasefire), shared by both factions with different flavour; 10 Ferryman trip lines; a tip line for each feature in the F-list.\n390\t\n391\t### 5.2 Dictations (six hidden tapes, the Notary's voice, subtitled)\n392\t\n393\t1. *Entry twelve. Forty crates to the Stewards on Tuesday. Forty to the Commons on Wednesday. On Friday the crates were opened on each other. I've checked the figures twice. They balance. They always balance. That is what frightens the clever ones.*\n394\t2. *Entry twenty-nine. A man came up the road to kill me. Good boots. I paid him twice what they were paying, and he shot the man who sent him. I've entered it under Sundries.*\n395\t3. *Entry thirty-three. People ask why I write it all down. A war with no records is only weather. I will not have this called weather.*\n396\t4. *Entry fifty-eight. The bark has stopped working on me. The Doctor says it isn't the fever any more, it's forty years of pit dust. I asked for that in writing.*\n397\t5. *Entry seventy-one. The Underwriters insure the Stewards against the Commons, and the Commons against the Stewards, at one rate, through one desk. I've met the man at the desk. He has a garden.*\n398\t6. *Entry ninety. You'll have found this in the strongroom, because I left it there. Come up to the Mission. Bring whoever's left. I have you down for Thursday.*\n399\t\n400\tTape 1 comes from C2's twist, tape 6 from C7. Tapes 2–5 are hidden in the world (a dead courier at `gp6`, the Signal Box, the capsized barge, the camp clerk's desk). Play through a small recorder, with the world still running.\n401\t\n402\t### 5.3 The campaign\n403\t\n404\t**Your job:** the Underwriters hired you to find a clerk called the Notary and bring back his ledger, or proof of death. You have no way in, so you take the work the country offers.\n405\t\n406\t**Prologue: The Barge** (dawn, walkable deck, 3–4 minutes, hold to skip).\n407\t- Down the Marrow past a burned bank, a wrecked patrol boat, zebra at the waterline. Three other mercs share the deck and needle each other.\n408\t- A Steward checkpoint launch stops you. An officer lays four passports on a table: **pick who you are** (`passport` focus by look, hover or D-pad). The other three are now your buddies.\n409\t- The Ferryman hands you the map: \"It's wrong, but it's wrong in useful ways.\"\n410\t- Land at the Landing with a first shiver. An Underwriters' agent in a clean shirt confirms your job and leaves on the same barge.\n411\t\n412\t**C1 First Wages** (the Widow, morning).\n413\t- A crate fell off a convoy at Junction. She lends you a rust-bucket pickup and a worn Service Pistol.\n414\t- Map up, set out. Two lazy guards at `gp1`. First fight, **forced jam**, first loot (a Carbine at condition 30), first surgery if hurt.\n415\t- Bring the crate back: 3 diamonds. She fits the locator to your GPS and points you at a case in the ditch by the Pump House. Shop opens. Sleep at the Pump House: choose an hour, save.\n416\t- Scripted engine hit on the next trip out: first repair.\n417\t\n418\t**C2 Dry Grass** (Comptroller). Burn the Commons' Fuel Dump in the Long Grass. He gives you a Flare Pistol: \"It's a signal flare. Signal something.\" Stewards' papers issued.\n419\t- *Beats:* drive out over Kiln Bridge (through or around `gp2`), climb the rise, monocular, read the wind, light the grass upwind. Three tanks must go. **Scripted wind shift** as the tanks blow: the front swings toward you, and you run or drive.\n420\t- *Twist (Tomasz, or the highest-trust merc you didn't pick):* \"There's a courier in that office with a satchel. Get him out before you light it, or don't light it till you have.\" Pay +3, tape 1, first mention of the Notary.\n421\t- *Consequences:* `gp2` flips to Stewards, a black scar across the Long Grass that stays. The camp's road is smoked (`camp.count` −12). The Doctor mentions it.\n422\t\n423\t**E1 Bark Run** (the Doctor, offered at first fever). Carry transit papers to Second Water: by skiff from below Kiln, or by ferry, or by truck through `gp7`. Meet the Clerk, who counts. See what your last job did. Reward: a bottle of 4 doses.\n424\t\n425\t**C3 Bad Bridge** (Foreman, night). Blow the rail span before the morning troop train. Commons' papers issued.\n426\t- *Beats:* skiff up the Marrow in the dark, guards with lamps, plant 3 charges on the piers (hold), get clear, detonate. The span falls in real physics (a cluster of dynamic bodies).\n427\t- *Twist (Dao):* \"There's a payroll car on that train. Wait for it. Blow it when it's on the span, and I'll meet you in the water.\" The train really crosses. Salvage the strongbox from the wreck under fire. Pay +3.\n428\t- *Consequences:* Stewards' eastern posts stop refilling. The rail was the camp's way out (`camp.count` −20, or +15 if you'd delivered E1 first: people left in time). The Widow's prices go up by 1 on heavy weapons (\"Bridge is out. Everything's dearer now.\").\n429\t\n430\t**C4 Salt Shed** (Ines, any time after E1). Take the Salt Shed: a stealth-friendly post at dusk, machete and monocular, tall grass to hide in. Reward: safehouse, +10 trust.\n431\t\n432\t**C5 Good Intentions** (Comptroller). Stop a Commons radio truck convoy on the Grass Road: ambush from a Technical, mounted gun, moving targets.\n433\t- *Twist (Sefton):* \"Stop it, don't burn it. The driver's an old friend. He knows where the Notary drops his tapes.\" Spare him: tape location and trust. Burn it: pay stays, tape stays hidden until you find it.\n434\t\n435\t**C6 Second Shift** (Foreman). Drive a dynamite truck through Steward posts to the Workings Gate, on forged papers. Bumps damage cargo, fire detonates it. The papers scene at `gp8` is at its tensest here: a sticky-handed sergeant might search you. `gp5` is next. Leave the truck at the gate and walk (it goes up on a timer), or drive it through.\n436\t\n437\t**E2 Second Bark Run** (Doctor, when you're low on doses). A Steward patrol is emptying a refugee truck on the road to Low Ford. Ignoring it costs nothing. Stepping in costs you the patrol's whole post, and `camp.count` +60.\n438\t\n439\t**C7 The Workings** (Day 3, dusk; both fixers call you in).\n440\t- **You must pick a side now** (`choice`, irreversible). Your side's squads assault; the other's defend the pit.\n441\t- Fight down the terraces: burn the dry brush on the upper levels, ride the conveyor, or use the service tunnel at night. Your highest-trust buddy joins you.\n442\t- In the strongroom: tape 6 and the ledger's key.\n443\t- **On the way out your buddy is hit and goes down. Mercy scene, always, the first time:** \"It's all right. I can count. I've got the minutes and they don't come out. You've got a syringe. Don't be polite.\"\n444\t- Your side now owns the map's posts.\n445\t\n446\t**C8 The Notary** (night, the Mission). Up the Switchback past deserters at `gp6`. He's at a desk with a lamp and the ledger, not armed, coughing. He talks while he sharpens a pencil, and you can walk around the room.\n447\t\n448\t> You're late. I had you down for Thursday. Sit, or don't. Everything's in the book. Who sold. Who bought. Who insured the buyer against the seller, and at what rate. You can read it out: the mast still works. Four minutes, if they let you have four minutes. Or take it down to the river. The Underwriters keep their word; it's the only thing they keep. Or there's a flare on the desk. The wind comes round at dawn. I've done the sums. I won't tell you how they come out. I've found people argue.\n449\t\n450\tThree endings, all built from existing systems:\n451\t\n452\t- **Read It Out (`ending_read`).** Start the transmitter and hold the church and mast for 4 minutes against squads from both sides (`hold_zone`). A surviving buddy with trust ≥ 60 comes to help; one below 60 comes for you, and has your mercy prompt too. The ledger reads out over the radio, in the Notary's voice, while you fight. At dawn the mast is down and you walk toward the camp. *Ledger: \"Account closed. No balance carried.\"*\n453\t- **Sell It (`ending_sell`).** Take the ledger down to the Landing by 06:00. A truck run through both sides' roadblocks and a burning Long Grass. The clean-shirt agent pays in full. You stand on the barge. A new merc comes aboard, and you are handed a recorder. Your hand presses Record. *\"Entry one.\"* The Ferryman, to the new merc: \"First time?\"\n454\t- **Burn It (`ending_burn`).** Light three marks along the ridge line as the wind comes round, walling both armies off from Second Water (`camp.count` keeps what you saved, and the burn costs the Grass). Run through your own fire. Rain comes at last. The ledger is ash. *Ledger: \"No records exist. Some people do.\"*\n455\t\n456\t**Epilogue:** a ledger page, big type, one line at a time, printed from world state: people at Second Water; buddies carried and written off; grass burned in hectares; doses taken; guns broken; who owns the Concession now. Then credits, then the title screen. The title scene remembers: the grass is black after Burn It, the mast is down after Read It, and there's a recorder on the rail after Sell It.\n457\t\n458\t---\n459\t\n460\t## 6. Multiplayer\n461\t\n462\tTASK.md requires following the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`). Read that page once. Fetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from the same folder (`vendor/session.js`, `tools/hub/`). Client 1.4.0 ✔ at planning time. The harness's checks are the spec. Facts that shape the design:\n463\t\n464\t- Mode **`shared-world`**, seats **`[1, 4]`**, own card (`card: true`).\n465\t- `session.js` goes in **unmodified as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`**. The hub checks it byte-for-byte; don't let esbuild touch it.\n466\t- Tags:\n467\t  ```html\n468\t  <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n469\t  <meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n470\t  <meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n471\t  <meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n472\t  <meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Get the case onto the barge before the grass burns\">\n473\t  <meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · Square/E use · D-pad up/M map\">\n474\t  ```\n475\t  Declaring 8 minutes makes the hard limit 12 (1.5 ×, never past 15). Don't set `hub:webgpu`: the game also runs on three's WebGL2 fallback (§13.4), and the hub then deals it to every browser.\n476\t- Also in `<head>`: `<title>TITLE — TAGLINE</title>`, `meta description`, `theme-color`, an inline `data:` icon, `<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Far Cry 2\">`.\n477\t\n478\t### 6.1 The round: \"The Job\"\n479\t\n480\tThe same world and systems, one self-contained 8-minute co-op contract in the Long Grass at golden hour. A round is `createSim({ scenario:'job', … })`. Seats map to the four mercs in order, with armband and name tag in the seat colour.\n481\t\n482\t1. **In (0:00–~3:00).** All start at Salt Jetty (150, 110, on the east bank just below Kiln Bridge) with two pickups. Objective: the strongbox at the Fuel Dump. `gp2` is in the way. You can go through, around, or light it up. 9 extra diamond cases nearby, with locators on. Each diamond is personal score.\n483\t2. **The Case (~3:00–~5:00).** Hold Use on the strongbox (12 s, split between players working it). The alarm sounds. A case appears. Its carrier can't sprint and uses sidearm only, and drops it when downed. Anyone can pick it up.\n484\t3. **Out (5:00–8:00).** The wind shifts. A Steward fire team lights a line across the plain, sweeping toward the river. Chase trucks come. Everyone has one fever attack at a seeded time and one dose. The barge leaves at 8:30, or when every living player is aboard, with or without the case.\n485\t- **Revive:** a downed player crawls and bleeds out over 45 s. Teammates hold Use for 3 s (a syringe from their pouch of 2) to get them up with the drag animation. With only one player in a round, one AI buddy (the next merc in seat order) comes along, run by the host.\n486\t- **Scale:** enemies × (0.6 + 0.2 × players).\n487\t- **Result:** `won` = case on the barge. `scores` = diamonds banked × 10 + 50 for the case if `won` + 15 per revive. Standings by score, players left behind tied last.\n488\t- `stats`: `Diamonds, Revives, Jams, Downs, Burned` (names ≤ 16 chars). `awards` (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40), for example \"Pulled Them Out\". Only the host calls `AIHub.finish`, with player ids only. A server copy isn't a player.\n489\t\n490\t### 6.2 Boot in a session\n491\t\n492\t```js\n493\t// src/main.js, first lines. The hello must go out at once (10 s limit in the harness).\n494\tif (window.AIHub?.active) bootSession(); else bootStandalone();\n495\t\n496\tasync function bootSession() {\n497\t  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n498\t  if (!info) return bootStandalone();          // no hub after all\n499\t  const sim = createSim({ scenario: 'job', seed: info.seed, players: info.players, /* … */ });\n500\t  AIHub.on('start', onStart); AIHub.on('message', onMessage); AIHub.on('leave', onLeave);\n501\t  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishNow(); });   // finish() within graceMs (5 s)\n502\t  AIHub.on('end', stopEverything);             // no input, no sends, sound off\n503\t  if (!info.server) { await createView(sim); showCard(info); }     // a server copy has no renderer, camera, input or audio\n504\t  AIHub.ready();                               // no key press, and fast: see below\n505\t}\n506\t```\n507\t\n508\t- **No title, attract, menus or dev mode in a session.** Options opens a small overlay that doesn't pause: resume, volumes, invert, glyphs. No quit. Ignore Options while Create is held (the hub's chord). **Nothing in the game is ever bound to Create, in any mode.**\n509\t- **Your card** is the game's own: an in-world still (the jetty at golden hour, the truck, the four passports on a crate), showing the game's name, each player in their colour with ready ticks, the goal, this player's controls, and the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle or a named key → `AIHub.answer('more')`. No menus, no choices, no `Math.random`. Keep the key handler live from before `ready()`: the harness presses Enter shortly after.\n510\t- **Timing:** `ready()` must arrive within 20 s **on 4 copies under software rendering** (✔ a skeleton took up to 6 s just for `renderer.init()` under that load). So build the sim, make the renderer, and don't wait for every pipeline: compile lazily, and keep the first view small. Measure it; aim for ≤ 12 s.\n511\t- **Rendering never starves the protocol.** Host sim and sends run on a timer, not rAF, and keep going when the tab is hidden. Under software rendering, frames can take seconds: if a frame takes > 500 ms, skip rendering until 250 ms after it finished, so `time-up` handling and sends always get the main thread.\n512\t- Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Use it for the shared clock and the barge's departure. The hub may pass a short `limitMs`: scale the job's clock to `min(510 s, limitMs − 30 s)`.\n513\t- `AIHub.rng(label)` for anything shared. The sim never uses `Math.random` anyway. Names always go in via `textContent`, never as HTML. No chat, emotes or custom names. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open` in a session, and nothing but the hub for network.\n514\t- **Graphics failure:** if `renderer.init()` rejects (no WebGPU or WebGL2), a plain DOM message and `AIHub.fail('no graphics')`.\n515\t\n516\t### 6.3 Netcode\n517\t\n518\tThe host runs NPCs, fire, pickups, objectives. Each copy runs **its own player immediately** and tells the host where it is, like the hub's `arena.html` example. Static world is identical on every copy from the seed.\n519\t\n520\tLimits: **20 messages/s per copy (burst 40), 16 KB each, unreliable messages over ~1200 bytes fragment and die whole.** So budget:\n521\t\n522\t| Msg | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Content |\n523\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n524\t| `me` | client → host (`to`) | no | 12/s | `at`, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, flags, and the vehicle pose if driving |\n525\t| `a` | client → host | yes | ≤ 6/s | Bundled actions: hit claims, interact, ignite, revive, pick up |\n526\t| `s` | host → all | no | 12/s | `at`, players, up to about 24 nearest NPCs (round-robin the rest), vehicles, wind. **JSON must stay under 1200 bytes:** integers, arrays not objects. Test asserts it |\n527\t| `f` | host → all | yes | 4/s | Fire deltas: newly burning and newly burnt cell runs |\n528\t| `e` | host → all | yes | 4/s | Bundled events: explosions, deaths, voice lines, pickups, objective steps, fever seeds, damage to players, the case |\n529\t\n530\t- Coalesce into one outbox per tick. `send()` returning `false` is a test failure. Keep sending `me` and `s` from `start` even when nothing changed, including on a server copy (the harness checks traffic flows both ways on every copy).\n531\t- Clients interpolate others 150 ms behind and take older-than-newest snapshots as dropped. Own player is corrected only on teleports.\n532\t- **Hits are claims:** the client's shot, the host's check (target alive, range plausible). Fire on clients is visual only, from `f`.\n533\t- **Leaving:** `leave` removes the avatar and drops whatever they carried. If the host goes, the hub voids the round and `end` arrives; show nothing extra. `end` always stops input, sends and audio.\n534\t\n535\t### 6.4 On its own, outside a hub\n536\t\n537\tOutside a session everything in this section is inert, and `Math.random` and storage are the page's own. The game must also **offer multiplayer on its own**, as TASK.md asks:\n538\t\n539\t- **Title → The Job** has two choices: **Go Alone** (you plus an AI buddy) and **Same Computer** (windows of this game on this computer join over a `BroadcastChannel`).\n540\t- `net/transport.js` is the one interface the game talks to, with two implementations: `HubTransport` wrapping `AIHub`, and `LinkTransport` (host beacon, join list, seats and colours, a clock offset, the same size and rate limits so behaviour matches).\n541\t- \"Host\" shows a big lobby with seats filling. \"Start\" counts down. Results show on the game's own ledger screen.\n542\t- The same screen says plainly: *Online play runs through AI Hub sessions.* Secondary window: `window.open(location.href)` is allowed here, and only here.\n543\t- ✔ `BroadcastChannel` connects two pages on `file://` in Chromium.\n544\t\n545\t---\n546\t\n547\t## 7. UI and UX\n548\t\n549\t### 7.1 Rules for 10 feet\n550\t\n551\t- Designed at 1920 × 1080, with everything scaled from viewport height. Minimum text 28 px at 1080p (subtitles 40, prompts 34, menu items 44, headers 72). Safe area 5%.\n552\t- At most **7 focusable things on a screen**, one idea per screen. No tables, no scroll lists, no tooltips, no tiny icons. A test audits font sizes, safe area and focusable counts.\n553\t- Ink panels at 70–85% behind text on bright scenes. Paper-white text, rust-orange accent. Fonts in §10.4.\n554\t- **The UI is one system** (`src/ui/`): a screen stack and a focus model. D-pad or left stick moves focus, Cross confirms, Circle backs out. Keyboard: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc. Mouse: hover moves focus, click confirms, right-click backs. Focus is always visible (ink underline plus rust marker), and always restored when you come back. Every action gives a sound and a rumble tick.\n555\t- **Boot:** a DOM loading screen with `TITLE` appears within the first moment, before any heavy work. Yield between world-build stages. Keys pressed during load are harmless.\n556\t- **Pad unplugged in play:** auto-pause with one big line and a resume prompt. A pad or key press carries on.\n557\t- **Prompts follow the last input used.** A `<glyph action=\"use\">` resolves to: PlayStation glyphs (default for pads), Xbox glyphs if Settings → Controller says so, or keycaps and mouse icons for keyboard and mouse. Draw all glyphs as inline SVG. The swap happens the moment another device is touched, and tests cover it. Never more than 2 prompts at once in play. Hold actions show a fill ring.\n558\t\n559\t### 7.2 Controls\n560\t\n561\tPad is the standard mapping: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad U/D/L/R, axes 0–1 left, 2–3 right. Radial deadzones, response curve, pad-only aim assist (slowdown within a 3° cone, slight pull on aim; toggle in Settings). Rumble through `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` with a guard.\n562\t\n563\t| On foot | Controller | Keyboard and mouse |\n564\t|---|---|---|\n565\t| Move / look | Left stick / right stick | WASD / mouse (pointer lock) |\n566\t| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | Left button / right button (hold) |\n567\t| Jump | Cross | Space |\n568\t| Crouch | Circle | C (toggle), Ctrl (hold) |\n569\t| Use; else reload or clear jam | Square | E use, R reload or clear jam |\n570\t| Next weapon (hold: pick) | Triangle | 1 2 3, wheel |\n571\t| Machete | R1 | F |\n572\t| Molotov | L1 | G |\n573\t| Sprint | L3 | Shift |\n574\t| Map | D-pad Up | M |\n575\t| Heal / surgery | D-pad Right | H |\n576\t| Take dose | D-pad Down | P |\n577\t| Monocular | D-pad Left | B |\n578\t| Notebook | Touchpad (button 17, if present) and in Pause | Tab |\n579\t| Pause | Options | Esc |\n580\t\n581\t| Driving | Controller | Keyboard and mouse |\n582\t|---|---|---|\n583\t| Throttle / brake or reverse | R2 / L2 | W / S |\n584\t| Steer / look | Left stick / right stick | A D / mouse |\n585\t| Handbrake | Cross | Space |\n586\t| Get out / gun seat | Square / Triangle | E / T |\n587\t| Horn / lights | R1 / Circle | H / L |\n588\t| Map | D-pad Up | M |\n589\t\n590\tInput matches `e.code` first and `e.key` as fallback (✔ the harness's synthetic keys send `code: 'a'`). Keyboard rebinding isn't required.\n591\t\n592\t**Mouse in the world.** In play, the crosshair *is* the hover: things you look at take focus (ink outline), and left-click activates them when your hands are empty or holstered (Kiln, the gun table, beds, doors). On the gun table, the map and passports, pointer lock is released: the cursor moves freely, hover focuses, click acts. Re-lock on return. If the browser refuses the lock, show a big \"Click to take the mouse\" prompt.\n593\t\n594\t### 7.3 HUD (fades when nothing is happening)\n595\t\n596\tBottom-left: 5 health bars and syringe count. Bottom-right: big ammo number and weapon icon (crack below 25 condition). Centre: small ink crosshair, detection arcs, hit ticks, damage arcs. Lower-centre: prompts. Upper-centre, briefly: objective line when it changes. Subtitles at the bottom. Nothing else: no minimap, no compass (the GPS and road signs do that), no quest arrows in the world.\n597\t\n598\t### 7.4 Screens\n599\t\n600\tEach is one calm screen:\n601\t\n602\t- **Title:** live in-engine scene, big title, Continue / New Game / The Job / Settings / About & Credits.\n603\t- **Pause:** Resume / Notebook / Settings / Dev Mode / About & Credits / Quit to Title.\n604\t- **Settings**, four pages by L1/R1:\n605\t  - *Sound:* Master, **Music (default 10%)**, Effects, Voices.\n606\t  - *Controller:* look speed, invert, aim assist, vibration, **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**.\n607\t  - *Mouse & Screen:* mouse speed, FOV, subtitles, text size, ink strength, fever effect strength, fullscreen.\n608\t  - *Game:* difficulty, and a head bob toggle.\n609\t- **Notebook:** one page at a time: the contract, what you know, who's alive, one tip.\n610\t- **Others:** contract sheet (a paper in your hand: three lines, Accept / Not now), gun table cards, bed watch, map focus, mercy choice, ledger pages (death, epilogue, job results), link lobby.\n611\t- **Difficulty:** Hired Hand / Veteran / Written Off, which scale incoming damage, pay and syringes.\n612\t\n613\t**Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` and not `(pointer: fine)`; ✔ `maxTouchPoints` is 0 on Playwright's WebKit iPhone, so don't use it): no touch controls. The title shows **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a big tappable **Settings** button, and nothing else playable. Attract mode runs. A key press or a connected pad unlocks the normal title. Settings is fully usable by tap.\n614\t\n615\t### 7.5 About & Credits\n616\t\n617\tReachable from Title and Pause. Paged, big type, one section per page (L1/R1, or left/right), reading from `src/data/about.json`:\n618\t\n619\t- **Source Information:** every field TASK.md lists, copied exactly, with `Usage` reading \"added on import\".\n620\t- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** every question and answer.\n621\t- **Credits:** three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), fonts and their licences, AI Hub session client.\n622\t\n623\t`tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview JSON beside the HTML from the same `about.json` and validates its shape, so they can't drift. Fill it last, rebuild once. Keep a running tally in `docs/issues-log.md` as you go, so the Testing Feedback counts are honest. Suggested `aiHub` block: type `Game`, genre `Shooter`, source `Far Cry 2`, series `Far Cry`, players `1–4`, tags `3d, first-person, co-op, story, exploration, vehicles`.\n624\t\n625\t---\n626\t\n627\t## 8. Attract mode\n628\t\n629\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on any front-end menu screen (not in play). Any key, mouse move or click, wheel, touch, pad button or stick > 0.3 exits to the same screen with focus intact. Resets the idle timer otherwise.\n630\t- **What runs:** the real sim and view, driven by `src/attract/director.js` from data (`src/data/attract.js`): a looping reel of vignettes, joined by ink wipes, with cheats on (god mode, infinite ammo, teleport, no clip, forced events). Small \"DEMO\" mark and a pulsing \"Press any button\" (or the touch message and Settings button on touch-only).\n631\t- **It runs in its own throwaway sim**, never touching the player's save or settings. Exit discards it and returns to the title scene.\n632\t- **Each vignette** states up to a few things it wants shown, so the reel is mostly genuine AI play: the bot moves, shoots, heals. About 25–35 s each, 6–7 minutes a loop. Together they cover at least 80% of the F-list:\n633\t\n634\t| # | Vignette | Shows |\n635\t|---|---|---|\n636\t| 1 | Kiln at morning: walk the market, gun holstered, the Widow's table, a buy, a fresh gun from the crate | `ceasefire_town`, `shop_buy`, `armoury_redraw` |\n637\t| 2 | Pickup at golden hour on the Grass Road, map up, focus to set a waypoint, GPS arrow | `drive`, `map_raise`, `map_focus`, `map_drive`, `gps_waypoint`, `day_night` |\n638\t| 3 | Checkpoint: papers out the window, waved on. Next post: \"Out of the truck.\" | `papers_ok`, `papers_fail` |\n639\t| 4 | Ridge at dusk: monocular, tag guards, flare into grass, front sweeps a post, herd bolts, tanks blow | `monocular_tag`, `flare_ignite`, `fire_spread`, `animals_flee`, `explosion_physics` |\n640\t| 5 | Firefight at Junction: a rusty gun jams, clears, then comes apart. Grab a looted carbine. Ragdolls, a man crawling, a comrade dragging him, post falls quiet | `rust_visual`, `jam`, `jam_clear`, `gun_break`, `loot_gun`, `ragdoll`, `wounded_crawl`, `comrade_drag`, `post_clear` |\n641\t| 6 | All four surgeries in cover, then a syringe | `surgery_bullet`, `surgery_finger`, `surgery_shrapnel`, `surgery_burn`, `heal_syringe` |\n642\t| 7 | Fever on the road: world warps, bottle, dose, recovery | `fever`, `pill` |\n643\t| 8 | Down in the dirt, buddy runs in, drag, pistol in hand. Then the buddy goes down: morphine | `rescue`, `buddy_down`, `mercy` |\n644\t| 9 | Ferry to Bridge Pier, skiff to the capsized barge, locator hunt, a case, a tape | `ferry`, `skiff`, `locator_found`, `diamond`, `dictation` |\n645\t| 10 | Engine hit, hood up, wrench under fire. Then a Technical on the mounted gun | `breakdown`, `repair`, `mounted_gun` |\n646\t| 11 | Night sneak through tall grass past lamp guards: machete, then a Molotov | `night_stealth`, `crouch_grass`, `machete_takedown`, `molotov` |\n647\t| 12 | Bed and watch, hands spin, light sweeps the shutters | `sleep_time` |\n648\t| 13 | The Tube at a truck, then the bridge goes with the train on it, chase-cam fly-by | `rocket`, `train`, `explosion_physics` |\n649\t| 14 | Wind turns, Drip Torch, wall of fire, trees burn, embers jump the road, title card | `torch_flame`, `wind_shift`, `tree_burn`, `ember_spot` |\n650\t\n651\tNo sound until the browser has had a gesture (AudioContext stays suspended, no error). Touch-only devices run it the same way.\n652\t\n653\t---\n654\t\n655\t## 9. Dev mode and tunables\n656\t\n657\t**Dev Mode** is an item in the Pause menu outside sessions, built with the same 10-foot UI, in pages by L1/R1.\n658\t\n659\t| Page | Tools |\n660\t|---|---|\n661\t| **Cheats** | God mode, infinite ammo, never jam, no clip / fly, one-hit kills, invisible to AI, time scale (0.1–4×), give all weapons, +10 diamonds, +4 doses, +3 syringes |\n662\t| **World** | Time of day dial, wind angle and speed, weather, ignite at crosshair, put out all fires, regrow all grass, clear post, refill post, spawn squad / truck / herd / crate here |\n663\t| **Trigger** | Fever now, go down now, buddy down, force jam, break gun, stall truck, papers check |\n664\t| **Jump** | Teleport to any place (big list, one page at a time), jump to any contract or set-piece start, any ending, complete current objective, reset save |\n665\t| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), with **Reset page** and **Reset all to defaults**. Values also print as JSON (\"Copy values\") |\n666\t| **Debug** | Overlays: physics lines, AI state labels, perception cones, nav grid, fire grid, smoke grid, frame stats, net stats. Dump state. Feature coverage (F-list seen or unseen) |\n667\t| **Place** | Designer helper: choose a prefab, place at crosshair, rotate, nudge, \"Copy as JSON\" to paste into `src/data/world.js` |\n668\t\n669\t**Tunables** (`src/data/tunables.js`: `{id, label, group, min, max, step, def}`). Every slider takes effect immediately in the running sim. Tests check a change takes effect and that reset restores defaults."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"81556622-e5f5-4864-b228-550dba7c5d86","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:47.855Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### 4.12 Factions and world state\n\n`world.state` holds: post owners and garrisons; `dump` and `railbridge` status; standing with each faction (−100..100, start 0); papers; `camp.count` (starts at 212, changed by your choices and consequences); buddy states; dictations found; chosen side; flags. Contract `onComplete` actions change it. Dialogue variants and the camp's look (crowded, thinning, ash on the tents) read it. The ending ledger prints from it.\n\n### 4.13 Contract runner\n\n`src/sim/contracts.js` runs declarative data from `src/data/contracts.js`.\n\n```js\n{ id:'c2', title:'Dry Grass', giver:'comptroller', requires:['c1'], side:'stewards', pay:6,\n  offer:['line id',…], twist:{ buddy:'tomasz', line:'…', pay:3, trust:10, steps:[…] },\n  steps:[ {do:'goto', poi:'dump', r:90, note:'…'}, {do:'destroy', tags:['dump_tank'], count:3},\n          {do:'return', npc:'comptroller'} ],\n  onComplete:[ {set:'post.gp2.owner', to:'stewards'}, {add:'standing.commons', by:-20},\n               {add:'camp.count', by:-12}, {ledger:'…'} ] }\n```\n\nStep vocabulary: `goto, talk, interact (hold), collect, destroy, kill, plant, survive, hold_zone, escort, deliver, drive_cargo, sleep_until, choice, wait_event`. Each step type is a small handler. Documented in `docs/DESIGNER.md`, validated by `tools/validate-data.mjs`.\n\n**Nothing dead-ends.** A failed contract (dynamite truck lost, target escaped) is re-offered after the next sleep at lower pay, with any lost vehicle or item re-issued. A contract that needs a destroyed thing to still exist re-checks world state first and adjusts. The bot playthrough tests one failure and retry.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Story and writing\n\n### 5.1 Voice (narrative tone)\n\nA weary, literate, morally exhausted voice, in the spirit of the source's Conrad-flavoured bleakness, with **our own rhetorical signature: bookkeeping**. Everyone talks about violence as accounts, shifts, invoices, rates, write-offs. Rules:\n\n- Short declarative sentences. People talk while doing something else, and they don't stop because you walked off.\n- Nobody explains the theme. Nobody winks. Humour is dry and dead-eyed.\n- No \"chosen one\". You're a line item and everyone knows it.\n- Subtitles are the only real language (voices are gibberish, §12). Two lines at most, big type.\n\n**Samples, to set the bar. Write the rest in this voice.**\n\n> **Ferryman:** First time? … Everyone says it's their last. Mostly they're right.\n>\n> **Widow:** New barrel, no rust, no history. That's more than you can say for anyone who's ever bought one.\n>\n> **Comptroller:** We don't say \"war\" in this office. We say \"adverse operating conditions\". You'll burn the Commons' diesel before Thursday. Invoice me for the matches.\n>\n> **Foreman:** My grandfather dug that pit. My father dug it deeper. I'm the first of us who gets to fill it.\n>\n> **Doctor:** Nothing here cures. It only moves the bill to next week.\n>\n> **Clerk of Second Water:** Two hundred and twelve this morning. You can tell whoever pays you that I counted.\n>\n> **Ines (rescue):** Don't look at it. Look at me. There. That's the worst of it over, and I'm lying.\n>\n> **Tomasz (rescue):** I said I'd come back for you. I also said that to my wife. Get up.\n>\n> **Dao (rescue):** You owe me four diamonds and a leg. Yours, if I have to carry you again.\n>\n> **Sefton (rescue):** Thirty years I've been leaving this place. Up you come.\n>\n> **Guards:** \"Wind's coming round! Leave it, leave it!\" · \"It's stuck, it's stuck!\" · \"Don't leave me for the birds.\" · \"Got you. Stop helping.\"\n\nWrite at least: 4 rescue lines per buddy; 12 lines per fixer; 20 guard barks per category (spotted, lost you, fire, jam, wounded, dragging, reload, ceasefire), shared by both factions with different flavour; 10 Ferryman trip lines; a tip line for each feature in the F-list.\n\n### 5.2 Dictations (six hidden tapes, the Notary's voice, subtitled)\n\n1. *Entry twelve. Forty crates to the Stewards on Tuesday. Forty to the Commons on Wednesday. On Friday the crates were opened on each other. I've checked the figures twice. They balance. They always balance. That is what frightens the clever ones.*\n2. *Entry twenty-nine. A man came up the road to kill me. Good boots. I paid him twice what they were paying, and he shot the man who sent him. I've entered it under Sundries.*\n3. *Entry thirty-three. People ask why I write it all down. A war with no records is only weather. I will not have this called weather.*\n4. *Entry fifty-eight. The bark has stopped working on me. The Doctor says it isn't the fever any more, it's forty years of pit dust. I asked for that in writing.*\n5. *Entry seventy-one. The Underwriters insure the Stewards against the Commons, and the Commons against the Stewards, at one rate, through one desk. I've met the man at the desk. He has a garden.*\n6. *Entry ninety. You'll have found this in the strongroom, because I left it there. Come up to the Mission. Bring whoever's left. I have you down for Thursday.*\n\nTape 1 comes from C2's twist, tape 6 from C7. Tapes 2–5 are hidden in the world (a dead courier at `gp6`, the Signal Box, the capsized barge, the camp clerk's desk). Play through a small recorder, with the world still running.\n\n### 5.3 The campaign\n\n**Your job:** the Underwriters hired you to find a clerk called the Notary and bring back his ledger, or proof of death. You have no way in, so you take the work the country offers.\n\n**Prologue: The Barge** (dawn, walkable deck, 3–4 minutes, hold to skip).\n- Down the Marrow past a burned bank, a wrecked patrol boat, zebra at the waterline. Three other mercs share the deck and needle each other.\n- A Steward checkpoint launch stops you. An officer lays four passports on a table: **pick who you are** (`passport` focus by look, hover or D-pad). The other three are now your buddies.\n- The Ferryman hands you the map: \"It's wrong, but it's wrong in useful ways.\"\n- Land at the Landing with a first shiver. An Underwriters' agent in a clean shirt confirms your job and leaves on the same barge.\n\n**C1 First Wages** (the Widow, morning).\n- A crate fell off a convoy at Junction. She lends you a rust-bucket pickup and a worn Service Pistol.\n- Map up, set out. Two lazy guards at `gp1`. First fight, **forced jam**, first loot (a Carbine at condition 30), first surgery if hurt.\n- Bring the crate back: 3 diamonds. She fits the locator to your GPS and points you at a case in the ditch by the Pump House. Shop opens. Sleep at the Pump House: choose an hour, save.\n- Scripted engine hit on the next trip out: first repair.\n\n**C2 Dry Grass** (Comptroller). Burn the Commons' Fuel Dump in the Long Grass. He gives you a Flare Pistol: \"It's a signal flare. Signal something.\" Stewards' papers issued.\n- *Beats:* drive out over Kiln Bridge (through or around `gp2`), climb the rise, monocular, read the wind, light the grass upwind. Three tanks must go. **Scripted wind shift** as the tanks blow: the front swings toward you, and you run or drive.\n- *Twist (Tomasz, or the highest-trust merc you didn't pick):* \"There's a courier in that office with a satchel. Get him out before you light it, or don't light it till you have.\" Pay +3, tape 1, first mention of the Notary.\n- *Consequences:* `gp2` flips to Stewards, a black scar across the Long Grass that stays. The camp's road is smoked (`camp.count` −12). The Doctor mentions it.\n\n**E1 Bark Run** (the Doctor, offered at first fever). Carry transit papers to Second Water: by skiff from below Kiln, or by ferry, or by truck through `gp7`. Meet the Clerk, who counts. See what your last job did. Reward: a bottle of 4 doses.\n\n**C3 Bad Bridge** (Foreman, night). Blow the rail span before the morning troop train. Commons' papers issued.\n- *Beats:* skiff up the Marrow in the dark, guards with lamps, plant 3 charges on the piers (hold), get clear, detonate. The span falls in real physics (a cluster of dynamic bodies).\n- *Twist (Dao):* \"There's a payroll car on that train. Wait for it. Blow it when it's on the span, and I'll meet you in the water.\" The train really crosses. Salvage the strongbox from the wreck under fire. Pay +3.\n- *Consequences:* Stewards' eastern posts stop refilling. The rail was the camp's way out (`camp.count` −20, or +15 if you'd delivered E1 first: people left in time). The Widow's prices go up by 1 on heavy weapons (\"Bridge is out. Everything's dearer now.\").\n\n**C4 Salt Shed** (Ines, any time after E1). Take the Salt Shed: a stealth-friendly post at dusk, machete and monocular, tall grass to hide in. Reward: safehouse, +10 trust.\n\n**C5 Good Intentions** (Comptroller). Stop a Commons radio truck convoy on the Grass Road: ambush from a Technical, mounted gun, moving targets.\n- *Twist (Sefton):* \"Stop it, don't burn it. The driver's an old friend. He knows where the Notary drops his tapes.\" Spare him: tape location and trust. Burn it: pay stays, tape stays hidden until you find it.\n\n**C6 Second Shift** (Foreman). Drive a dynamite truck through Steward posts to the Workings Gate, on forged papers. Bumps damage cargo, fire detonates it. The papers scene at `gp8` is at its tensest here: a sticky-handed sergeant might search you. `gp5` is next. Leave the truck at the gate and walk (it goes up on a timer), or drive it through.\n\n**E2 Second Bark Run** (Doctor, when you're low on doses). A Steward patrol is emptying a refugee truck on the road to Low Ford. Ignoring it costs nothing. Stepping in costs you the patrol's whole post, and `camp.count` +60.\n\n**C7 The Workings** (Day 3, dusk; both fixers call you in).\n- **You must pick a side now** (`choice`, irreversible). Your side's squads assault; the other's defend the pit.\n- Fight down the terraces: burn the dry brush on the upper levels, ride the conveyor, or use the service tunnel at night. Your highest-trust buddy joins you.\n- In the strongroom: tape 6 and the ledger's key.\n- **On the way out your buddy is hit and goes down. Mercy scene, always, the first time:** \"It's all right. I can count. I've got the minutes and they don't come out. You've got a syringe. Don't be polite.\"\n- Your side now owns the map's posts.\n\n**C8 The Notary** (night, the Mission). Up the Switchback past deserters at `gp6`. He's at a desk with a lamp and the ledger, not armed, coughing. He talks while he sharpens a pencil, and you can walk around the room.\n\n> You're late. I had you down for Thursday. Sit, or don't. Everything's in the book. Who sold. Who bought. Who insured the buyer against the seller, and at what rate. You can read it out: the mast still works. Four minutes, if they let you have four minutes. Or take it down to the river. The Underwriters keep their word; it's the only thing they keep. Or there's a flare on the desk. The wind comes round at dawn. I've done the sums. I won't tell you how they come out. I've found people argue.\n\nThree endings, all built from existing systems:\n\n- **Read It Out (`ending_read`).** Start the transmitter and hold the church and mast for 4 minutes against squads from both sides (`hold_zone`). A surviving buddy with trust ≥ 60 comes to help; one below 60 comes for you, and has your mercy prompt too. The ledger reads out over the radio, in the Notary's voice, while you fight. At dawn the mast is down and you walk toward the camp. *Ledger: \"Account closed. No balance carried.\"*\n- **Sell It (`ending_sell`).** Take the ledger down to the Landing by 06:00. A truck run through both sides' roadblocks and a burning Long Grass. The clean-shirt agent pays in full. You stand on the barge. A new merc comes aboard, and you are handed a recorder. Your hand presses Record. *\"Entry one.\"* The Ferryman, to the new merc: \"First time?\"\n- **Burn It (`ending_burn`).** Light three marks along the ridge line as the wind comes round, walling both armies off from Second Water (`camp.count` keeps what you saved, and the burn costs the Grass). Run through your own fire. Rain comes at last. The ledger is ash. *Ledger: \"No records exist. Some people do.\"*\n\n**Epilogue:** a ledger page, big type, one line at a time, printed from world state: people at Second Water; buddies carried and written off; grass burned in hectares; doses taken; guns broken; who owns the Concession now. Then credits, then the title screen. The title scene remembers: the grass is black after Burn It, the mast is down after Read It, and there's a recorder on the rail after Sell It.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Multiplayer\n\nTASK.md requires following the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`). Read that page once. Fetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from the same folder (`vendor/session.js`, `tools/hub/`). Client 1.4.0 ✔ at planning time. The harness's checks are the spec. Facts that shape the design:\n\n- Mode **`shared-world`**, seats **`[1, 4]`**, own card (`card: true`).\n- `session.js` goes in **unmodified as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`**. The hub checks it byte-for-byte; don't let esbuild touch it.\n- Tags:\n  ```html\n  <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n  <meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n  <meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n  <meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n  <meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Get the case onto the barge before the grass burns\">\n  <meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · Square/E use · D-pad up/M map\">\n  ```\n  Declaring 8 minutes makes the hard limit 12 (1.5 ×, never past 15). Don't set `hub:webgpu`: the game also runs on three's WebGL2 fallback (§13.4), and the hub then deals it to every browser.\n- Also in `<head>`: `<title>TITLE — TAGLINE</title>`, `meta description`, `theme-color`, an inline `data:` icon, `<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Far Cry 2\">`.\n\n### 6.1 The round: \"The Job\"\n\nThe same world and systems, one self-contained 8-minute co-op contract in the Long Grass at golden hour. A round is `createSim({ scenario:'job', … })`. Seats map to the four mercs in order, with armband and name tag in the seat colour.\n\n1. **In (0:00–~3:00).** All start at Salt Jetty (150, 110, on the east bank just below Kiln Bridge) with two pickups. Objective: the strongbox at the Fuel Dump. `gp2` is in the way. You can go through, around, or light it up. 9 extra diamond cases nearby, with locators on. Each diamond is personal score.\n2. **The Case (~3:00–~5:00).** Hold Use on the strongbox (12 s, split between players working it). The alarm sounds. A case appears. Its carrier can't sprint and uses sidearm only, and drops it when downed. Anyone can pick it up.\n3. **Out (5:00–8:00).** The wind shifts. A Steward fire team lights a line across the plain, sweeping toward the river. Chase trucks come. Everyone has one fever attack at a seeded time and one dose. The barge leaves at 8:30, or when every living player is aboard, with or without the case.\n- **Revive:** a downed player crawls and bleeds out over 45 s. Teammates hold Use for 3 s (a syringe from their pouch of 2) to get them up with the drag animation. With only one player in a round, one AI buddy (the next merc in seat order) comes along, run by the host.\n- **Scale:** enemies × (0.6 + 0.2 × players).\n- **Result:** `won` = case on the barge. `scores` = diamonds banked × 10 + 50 for the case if `won` + 15 per revive. Standings by score, players left behind tied last.\n- `stats`: `Diamonds, Revives, Jams, Downs, Burned` (names ≤ 16 chars). `awards` (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40), for example \"Pulled Them Out\". Only the host calls `AIHub.finish`, with player ids only. A server copy isn't a player.\n\n### 6.2 Boot in a session\n\n```js\n// src/main.js, first lines. The hello must go out at once (10 s limit in the harness).\nif (window.AIHub?.active) bootSession(); else bootStandalone();\n\nasync function bootSession() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (!info) return bootStandalone();          // no hub after all\n  const sim = createSim({ scenario: 'job', seed: info.seed, players: info.players, /* … */ });\n  AIHub.on('start', onStart); AIHub.on('message', onMessage); AIHub.on('leave', onLeave);\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishNow(); });   // finish() within graceMs (5 s)\n  AIHub.on('end', stopEverything);             // no input, no sends, sound off\n  if (!info.server) { await createView(sim); showCard(info); }     // a server copy has no renderer, camera, input or audio\n  AIHub.ready();                               // no key press, and fast: see below\n}\n```\n\n- **No title, attract, menus or dev mode in a session.** Options opens a small overlay that doesn't pause: resume, volumes, invert, glyphs. No quit. Ignore Options while Create is held (the hub's chord). **Nothing in the game is ever bound to Create, in any mode.**\n- **Your card** is the game's own: an in-world still (the jetty at golden hour, the truck, the four passports on a crate), showing the game's name, each player in their colour with ready ticks, the goal, this player's controls, and the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle or a named key → `AIHub.answer('more')`. No menus, no choices, no `Math.random`. Keep the key handler live from before `ready()`: the harness presses Enter shortly after.\n- **Timing:** `ready()` must arrive within 20 s **on 4 copies under software rendering** (✔ a skeleton took up to 6 s just for `renderer.init()` under that load). So build the sim, make the renderer, and don't wait for every pipeline: compile lazily, and keep the first view small. Measure it; aim for ≤ 12 s.\n- **Rendering never starves the protocol.** Host sim and sends run on a timer, not rAF, and keep going when the tab is hidden. Under software rendering, frames can take seconds: if a frame takes > 500 ms, skip rendering until 250 ms after it finished, so `time-up` handling and sends always get the main thread.\n- Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Use it for the shared clock and the barge's departure. The hub may pass a short `limitMs`: scale the job's clock to `min(510 s, limitMs − 30 s)`.\n- `AIHub.rng(label)` for anything shared. The sim never uses `Math.random` anyway. Names always go in via `textContent`, never as HTML. No chat, emotes or custom names. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open` in a session, and nothing but the hub for network.\n- **Graphics failure:** if `renderer.init()` rejects (no WebGPU or WebGL2), a plain DOM message and `AIHub.fail('no graphics')`.\n\n### 6.3 Netcode\n\nThe host runs NPCs, fire, pickups, objectives. Each copy runs **its own player immediately** and tells the host where it is, like the hub's `arena.html` example. Static world is identical on every copy from the seed.\n\nLimits: **20 messages/s per copy (burst 40), 16 KB each, unreliable messages over ~1200 bytes fragment and die whole.** So budget:\n\n| Msg | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Content |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `me` | client → host (`to`) | no | 12/s | `at`, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, flags, and the vehicle pose if driving |\n| `a` | client → host | yes | ≤ 6/s | Bundled actions: hit claims, interact, ignite, revive, pick up |\n| `s` | host → all | no | 12/s | `at`, players, up to about 24 nearest NPCs (round-robin the rest), vehicles, wind. **JSON must stay under 1200 bytes:** integers, arrays not objects. Test asserts it |\n| `f` | host → all | yes | 4/s | Fire deltas: newly burning and newly burnt cell runs |\n| `e` | host → all | yes | 4/s | Bundled events: explosions, deaths, voice lines, pickups, objective steps, fever seeds, damage to players, the case |\n\n- Coalesce into one outbox per tick. `send()` returning `false` is a test failure. Keep sending `me` and `s` from `start` even when nothing changed, including on a server copy (the harness checks traffic flows both ways on every copy).\n- Clients interpolate others 150 ms behind and take older-than-newest snapshots as dropped. Own player is corrected only on teleports.\n- **Hits are claims:** the client's shot, the host's check (target alive, range plausible). Fire on clients is visual only, from `f`.\n- **Leaving:** `leave` removes the avatar and drops whatever they carried. If the host goes, the hub voids the round and `end` arrives; show nothing extra. `end` always stops input, sends and audio.\n\n### 6.4 On its own, outside a hub\n\nOutside a session everything in this section is inert, and `Math.random` and storage are the page's own. The game must also **offer multiplayer on its own**, as TASK.md asks:\n\n- **Title → The Job** has two choices: **Go Alone** (you plus an AI buddy) and **Same Computer** (windows of this game on this computer join over a `BroadcastChannel`).\n- `net/transport.js` is the one interface the game talks to, with two implementations: `HubTransport` wrapping `AIHub`, and `LinkTransport` (host beacon, join list, seats and colours, a clock offset, the same size and rate limits so behaviour matches).\n- \"Host\" shows a big lobby with seats filling. \"Start\" counts down. Results show on the game's own ledger screen.\n- The same screen says plainly: *Online play runs through AI Hub sessions.* Secondary window: `window.open(location.href)` is allowed here, and only here.\n- ✔ `BroadcastChannel` connects two pages on `file://` in Chromium.\n\n---\n\n## 7. UI and UX\n\n### 7.1 Rules for 10 feet\n\n- Designed at 1920 × 1080, with everything scaled from viewport height. Minimum text 28 px at 1080p (subtitles 40, prompts 34, menu items 44, headers 72). Safe area 5%.\n- At most **7 focusable things on a screen**, one idea per screen. No tables, no scroll lists, no tooltips, no tiny icons. A test audits font sizes, safe area and focusable counts.\n- Ink panels at 70–85% behind text on bright scenes. Paper-white text, rust-orange accent. Fonts in §10.4.\n- **The UI is one system** (`src/ui/`): a screen stack and a focus model. D-pad or left stick moves focus, Cross confirms, Circle backs out. Keyboard: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc. Mouse: hover moves focus, click confirms, right-click backs. Focus is always visible (ink underline plus rust marker), and always restored when you come back. Every action gives a sound and a rumble tick.\n- **Boot:** a DOM loading screen with `TITLE` appears within the first moment, before any heavy work. Yield between world-build stages. Keys pressed during load are harmless.\n- **Pad unplugged in play:** auto-pause with one big line and a resume prompt. A pad or key press carries on.\n- **Prompts follow the last input used.** A `<glyph action=\"use\">` resolves to: PlayStation glyphs (default for pads), Xbox glyphs if Settings → Controller says so, or keycaps and mouse icons for keyboard and mouse. Draw all glyphs as inline SVG. The swap happens the moment another device is touched, and tests cover it. Never more than 2 prompts at once in play. Hold actions show a fill ring.\n\n### 7.2 Controls\n\nPad is the standard mapping: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad U/D/L/R, axes 0–1 left, 2–3 right. Radial deadzones, response curve, pad-only aim assist (slowdown within a 3° cone, slight pull on aim; toggle in Settings). Rumble through `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` with a guard.\n\n| On foot | Controller | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move / look | Left stick / right stick | WASD / mouse (pointer lock) |\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | Left button / right button (hold) |\n| Jump | Cross | Space |\n| Crouch | Circle | C (toggle), Ctrl (hold) |\n| Use; else reload or clear jam | Square | E use, R reload or clear jam |\n| Next weapon (hold: pick) | Triangle | 1 2 3, wheel |\n| Machete | R1 | F |\n| Molotov | L1 | G |\n| Sprint | L3 | Shift |\n| Map | D-pad Up | M |\n| Heal / surgery | D-pad Right | H |\n| Take dose | D-pad Down | P |\n| Monocular | D-pad Left | B |\n| Notebook | Touchpad (button 17, if present) and in Pause | Tab |\n| Pause | Options | Esc |\n\n| Driving | Controller | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Throttle / brake or reverse | R2 / L2 | W / S |\n| Steer / look | Left stick / right stick | A D / mouse |\n| Handbrake | Cross | Space |\n| Get out / gun seat | Square / Triangle | E / T |\n| Horn / lights | R1 / Circle | H / L |\n| Map | D-pad Up | M |\n\nInput matches `e.code` first and `e.key` as fallback (✔ the harness's synthetic keys send `code: 'a'`). Keyboard rebinding isn't required.\n\n**Mouse in the world.** In play, the crosshair *is* the hover: things you look at take focus (ink outline), and left-click activates them when your hands are empty or holstered (Kiln, the gun table, beds, doors). On the gun table, the map and passports, pointer lock is released: the cursor moves freely, hover focuses, click acts. Re-lock on return. If the browser refuses the lock, show a big \"Click to take the mouse\" prompt.\n\n### 7.3 HUD (fades when nothing is happening)\n\nBottom-left: 5 health bars and syringe count. Bottom-right: big ammo number and weapon icon (crack below 25 condition). Centre: small ink crosshair, detection arcs, hit ticks, damage arcs. Lower-centre: prompts. Upper-centre, briefly: objective line when it changes. Subtitles at the bottom. Nothing else: no minimap, no compass (the GPS and road signs do that), no quest arrows in the world.\n\n### 7.4 Screens\n\nEach is one calm screen:\n\n- **Title:** live in-engine scene, big title, Continue / New Game / The Job / Settings / About & Credits.\n- **Pause:** Resume / Notebook / Settings / Dev Mode / About & Credits / Quit to Title.\n- **Settings**, four pages by L1/R1:\n  - *Sound:* Master, **Music (default 10%)**, Effects, Voices.\n  - *Controller:* look speed, invert, aim assist, vibration, **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**.\n  - *Mouse & Screen:* mouse speed, FOV, subtitles, text size, ink strength, fever effect strength, fullscreen.\n  - *Game:* difficulty, and a head bob toggle.\n- **Notebook:** one page at a time: the contract, what you know, who's alive, one tip.\n- **Others:** contract sheet (a paper in your hand: three lines, Accept / Not now), gun table cards, bed watch, map focus, mercy choice, ledger pages (death, epilogue, job results), link lobby.\n- **Difficulty:** Hired Hand / Veteran / Written Off, which scale incoming damage, pay and syringes.\n\n**Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` and not `(pointer: fine)`; ✔ `maxTouchPoints` is 0 on Playwright's WebKit iPhone, so don't use it): no touch controls. The title shows **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a big tappable **Settings** button, and nothing else playable. Attract mode runs. A key press or a connected pad unlocks the normal title. Settings is fully usable by tap.\n\n### 7.5 About & Credits\n\nReachable from Title and Pause. Paged, big type, one section per page (L1/R1, or left/right), reading from `src/data/about.json`:\n\n- **Source Information:** every field TASK.md lists, copied exactly, with `Usage` reading \"added on import\".\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** every question and answer.\n- **Credits:** three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), fonts and their licences, AI Hub session client.\n\n`tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview JSON beside the HTML from the same `about.json` and validates its shape, so they can't drift. Fill it last, rebuild once. Keep a running tally in `docs/issues-log.md` as you go, so the Testing Feedback counts are honest. Suggested `aiHub` block: type `Game`, genre `Shooter`, source `Far Cry 2`, series `Far Cry`, players `1–4`, tags `3d, first-person, co-op, story, exploration, vehicles`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Attract mode\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on any front-end menu screen (not in play). Any key, mouse move or click, wheel, touch, pad button or stick > 0.3 exits to the same screen with focus intact. Resets the idle timer otherwise.\n- **What runs:** the real sim and view, driven by `src/attract/director.js` from data (`src/data/attract.js`): a looping reel of vignettes, joined by ink wipes, with cheats on (god mode, infinite ammo, teleport, no clip, forced events). Small \"DEMO\" mark and a pulsing \"Press any button\" (or the touch message and Settings button on touch-only).\n- **It runs in its own throwaway sim**, never touching the player's save or settings. Exit discards it and returns to the title scene.\n- **Each vignette** states up to a few things it wants shown, so the reel is mostly genuine AI play: the bot moves, shoots, heals. About 25–35 s each, 6–7 minutes a loop. Together they cover at least 80% of the F-list:\n\n| # | Vignette | Shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Kiln at morning: walk the market, gun holstered, the Widow's table, a buy, a fresh gun from the crate | `ceasefire_town`, `shop_buy`, `armoury_redraw` |\n| 2 | Pickup at golden hour on the Grass Road, map up, focus to set a waypoint, GPS arrow | `drive`, `map_raise`, `map_focus`, `map_drive`, `gps_waypoint`, `day_night` |\n| 3 | Checkpoint: papers out the window, waved on. Next post: \"Out of the truck.\" | `papers_ok`, `papers_fail` |\n| 4 | Ridge at dusk: monocular, tag guards, flare into grass, front sweeps a post, herd bolts, tanks blow | `monocular_tag`, `flare_ignite`, `fire_spread`, `animals_flee`, `explosion_physics` |\n| 5 | Firefight at Junction: a rusty gun jams, clears, then comes apart. Grab a looted carbine. Ragdolls, a man crawling, a comrade dragging him, post falls quiet | `rust_visual`, `jam`, `jam_clear`, `gun_break`, `loot_gun`, `ragdoll`, `wounded_crawl`, `comrade_drag`, `post_clear` |\n| 6 | All four surgeries in cover, then a syringe | `surgery_bullet`, `surgery_finger`, `surgery_shrapnel`, `surgery_burn`, `heal_syringe` |\n| 7 | Fever on the road: world warps, bottle, dose, recovery | `fever`, `pill` |\n| 8 | Down in the dirt, buddy runs in, drag, pistol in hand. Then the buddy goes down: morphine | `rescue`, `buddy_down`, `mercy` |\n| 9 | Ferry to Bridge Pier, skiff to the capsized barge, locator hunt, a case, a tape | `ferry`, `skiff`, `locator_found`, `diamond`, `dictation` |\n| 10 | Engine hit, hood up, wrench under fire. Then a Technical on the mounted gun | `breakdown`, `repair`, `mounted_gun` |\n| 11 | Night sneak through tall grass past lamp guards: machete, then a Molotov | `night_stealth`, `crouch_grass`, `machete_takedown`, `molotov` |\n| 12 | Bed and watch, hands spin, light sweeps the shutters | `sleep_time` |\n| 13 | The Tube at a truck, then the bridge goes with the train on it, chase-cam fly-by | `rocket`, `train`, `explosion_physics` |\n| 14 | Wind turns, Drip Torch, wall of fire, trees burn, embers jump the road, title card | `torch_flame`, `wind_shift`, `tree_burn`, `ember_spot` |\n\nNo sound until the browser has had a gesture (AudioContext stays suspended, no error). Touch-only devices run it the same way.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Dev mode and tunables\n\n**Dev Mode** is an item in the Pause menu outside sessions, built with the same 10-foot UI, in pages by L1/R1.\n\n| Page | Tools |\n|---|---|\n| **Cheats** | God mode, infinite ammo, never jam, no clip / fly, one-hit kills, invisible to AI, time scale (0.1–4×), give all weapons, +10 diamonds, +4 doses, +3 syringes |\n| **World** | Time of day dial, wind angle and speed, weather, ignite at crosshair, put out all fires, regrow all grass, clear post, refill post, spawn squad / truck / herd / crate here |\n| **Trigger** | Fever now, go down now, buddy down, force jam, break gun, stall truck, papers check |\n| **Jump** | Teleport to any place (big list, one page at a time), jump to any contract or set-piece start, any ending, complete current objective, reset save |\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), with **Reset page** and **Reset all to defaults**. Values also print as JSON (\"Copy values\") |\n| **Debug** | Overlays: physics lines, AI state labels, perception cones, nav grid, fire grid, smoke grid, frame stats, net stats. Dump state. Feature coverage (F-list seen or unseen) |\n| **Place** | Designer helper: choose a prefab, place at crosshair, rotate, nudge, \"Copy as JSON\" to paste into `src/data/world.js` |\n\n**Tunables** (`src/data/tunables.js`: `{id, label, group, min, max, step, def}`). Every slider takes effect immediately in the running sim. Tests check a change takes effect and that reset restores defaults.","numLines":340,"startLine":330,"totalLines":1189}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EoQytRn1ACmqR4L86LqASs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
