{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCqFTH3hKPa46QTi25g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XWR5iPCjiPqHvkQ6J2GWTw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, ('MISSING: '+old[:90])\n    s=s.replace(old,new,1)\n\n# --- 6.2 boot: replace the code block and the first bullets\na=s.index(\"### 6.2 Boot in a session\")\nb=s.index(\"- Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"### 6.2 Boot in a session\n\n**Why this order matters.** In the harness every copy is a same-origin iframe, so **all copies share one main thread**. ✔ A skeleton that rendered while loading **failed** the hub's default run (no WebGPU flags, 4 copies, main-thread WebGL2 in software): the ready deadline was missed, `time-up`'s 5 s grace was missed, and the round went void. ✔ With the order below, all copies were ready in about 0.25 s, and every case passed with and without flags. Keep this order.\n\nIn the built `<head>`, right after `session.js`, so the hello goes out before the big bundle has even parsed (10 s limit):\n\n```html\n<script>if (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });</script>\n```\n\n```js\n// src/main.js\nif (window.AIHub?.active) bootSession(); else bootStandalone();\n\nasync function bootSession() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });  // the same promise as above\n  if (!info) return bootStandalone();          // no hub after all\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage); AIHub.on('leave', onLeave); AIHub.on('card', onCard);\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishNow(); });   // finish() within graceMs (5 s)\n  AIHub.on('end', stopEverything);             // no input, no sends, sound off\n  const sim = await createSim({ scenario: 'job', seed: info.seed, players: info.players, /* … */ });  // yield between stages\n  if (!info.server) showCard(info);            // DOM and Canvas2D only\n  AIHub.ready();                               // now: the sim is what must be ready. No key press\n  if (info.server) return startSimTimer();     // a server copy has no renderer, camera, input or audio\n  const view = await createView(sim);          // renderer.init(), scene built, NO frame yet\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { startSimTimer(); setTimeout(async () => {\n    await view.renderer.compileAsync(view.scene, view.camera);\n    view.startFrames();                        // through the governor below\n  }, AIHub.me * 800); });                      // stagger the copies\n}\n```\n\n- **No 3D frame before `start`.** The card is DOM and Canvas2D.\n- **Frame governor, in sessions.** If a frame took over 250 ms of main-thread time, wait `max(1000, min(4000, took × 3))` ms before the next. On a real GPU this never triggers.\n- **Sim and sends run on a timer, not rAF**, and keep going when the tab is hidden. After `start`, keep every main-thread task short: `time-up` must reach `finish()` inside 5 s even with four copies on one thread.\n- Measure on 4 copies with the real world build: `ready()` must arrive within the harness's 20 s, and aim for ≤ 12 s.\n- **No title, attract, menus or dev mode in a session.** Options opens a small overlay that doesn't pause: resume, volumes, invert, glyphs. No quit. Ignore Options while Create is held (the hub's chord). **Nothing in the game is ever bound to Create, in any mode.**\n- **Your card** is the game's own: a 2D ink composition (the jetty at golden hour, the truck, four passports on a crate), showing the game's name, each player in their colour with ready ticks, the goal, this player's controls, and the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle or a named key → `AIHub.answer('more')`. No menus, no choices, no `Math.random`. Keep the key handler live from before `ready()`: the harness presses Enter shortly after.\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\n\n# Claim in the hub tier\nrep(\"HARNESS_CLAIM\",\"✔ All six pass on a skeleton with the flags. With no flags, the 4-player, host-leave and server cases pass too, using the §6.2 boot order.\")\n\n# 13.6 HTML includes the early hello\nrep(\"\"\"<script>…vendor/session.js exactly…</script>\n<title>…</title> …metas… <style>…</style>\"\"\",\"\"\"<script>…vendor/session.js exactly…</script>\n<script>…the early connect() from §6.2…</script>\n<title>…</title> …metas… <style>…</style>\"\"\")\n\n# Flashlight\nrep(\"30 m at night (the player's flashlight or a nearby fire raises it).\",\"30 m at night (standing near a fire or lamp, or driving with headlights on, raises it).\")\n\n# E2 text\nrep(\"Ignoring it costs nothing. Stepping in costs you the patrol's whole post, and `camp.count` +60.\",\n    \"Ignoring it costs nothing. Stepping in means a fight, your Stewards' papers burned until dawn, and `camp.count` +60.\")\n\n# Dev pages obey the 10-foot rule\nrep(\"**Dev Mode** is an item in the Pause menu outside sessions, built with the same 10-foot UI, in pages by L1/R1.\",\n    \"**Dev Mode** is an item in the Pause menu outside sessions, built with the same 10-foot UI, in pages by L1/R1. Long pages split into sub-pages of at most 7 rows (D-pad left and right), so the balance groups below are one sub-page each. A hotkey isn't needed, but F1 opens it directly on keyboard.\")\n\n# C4 follows the substitution rule\nrep(\"Each twist names a default merc. If that merc is you, or dead, the next living buddy by trust takes the same lines, so write them to fit anyone.\",\n    \"Each twist (and C4, which a buddy gives) names a default merc. If that merc is you, or dead, the next living buddy by trust takes the same lines, so write them to fit anyone.\")\n\n# Lockfile wording\nrep(\"`npm install` in the dev folder, and commit `package-lock.json`.\",\"`npm install` in the dev folder, and keep `package-lock.json`.\")\n\n# Tab hidden, audio unlock\nrep(\"- **Pad unplugged in play:** auto-pause with one big line and a resume prompt. A pad or key press carries on.\",\n    \"- **Pad unplugged, or tab hidden, in play (outside sessions):** auto-pause with one big line and a resume prompt. A pad or key press carries on.\")\nrep(\"- **Title:** live in-engine scene, big title, Continue / New Game / The Job / Settings / About & Credits.\",\n    \"- **Title:** live in-engine scene, big title, Continue (when a save exists) / New Game / The Job / Settings / About & Credits. The first input of any kind resumes the AudioContext.\")\n\n# Driving table\nrep(\"| Horn / lights | R1 / Circle | H / L |\\n| Map | D-pad Up | M |\",\n    \"| Horn / lights | R1 / Circle | Q / L |\\n| Map | D-pad Up | M |\\n| Heal / dose | D-pad Right / D-pad Down | H / P |\\n| Molotov from the window | L1 | G |\\n| Radio | D-pad Left | R |\")\n\n# const\nrep(\"fireMat = new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ side: THREE.DoubleSide });\",\"const fireMat = new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ side: THREE.DoubleSide });\")\n\n# Attract test fast-forward\nrep(\"- Attract: starts between 10 and 11 s idle on title; any of key, mouse, button or stick exits with focus intact; loops past a full cycle; coverage ≥ 80%.\",\n    \"- Attract: starts between 10 and 11 s idle on title; any of key, mouse, button or stick exits with focus intact; loops past a full cycle (fast-forward with `__game.step`); coverage ≥ 80%; a save made beforehand is untouched.\")\n\n# Memory note\nrep(\"- Run one browser at a time. A 4-copy harness run is one browser but heavy. \\\"Target closed\\\" means out of memory; lower the load, don't retry blindly.\",\n    \"- Run one browser at a time (20 GB of RAM, shared; earlyoom ends the biggest browser). A 4-copy harness run is one browser but heavy. \\\"Target closed\\\" means out of memory; lower the load, don't retry blindly.\")\n\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\n# Coverage check: every attract id is in the F-list, and the share is at least 80%.\nimport re\nflist=re.search(r\"`(fire_spread [^`]+)`\",s).group(1).split()\nreel=s[s.index(\"| # | Vignette | Shows |\"):s.index(\"No sound until the browser has had a gesture\")]\nids=set()\nfor line in reel.splitlines():\n    if line.startswith('|') and line.count('|')>=4:\n        ids.update(re.findall(r\"`([a-z_]+)`\",line.rsplit('|',2)[1]))\nprint('F-list',len(flist),'attract',len(ids),'share',round(len(ids)/len(flist)*100,1),'unknown ids',sorted(ids-set(flist)))\nprint('not in attract:',sorted(set(flist)-ids))\nprint('banned scan:',re.findall(r\"exit-interview\\.json|GameTitle|claude-opus|20261104|HARNESS_CLAIM|TODO:\",s))\nprint('words',len(s.split()),'lines',s.count(chr(10)))\nEOF","description":"Record the boot order and final fixes, then check coverage"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2133,"cache_read_input_tokens":415469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2133},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"d4ce8375-af72-4f60-8094-ced3a3927032","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:40.757Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCqFAQtn8W6i3d9n5zL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XWR5iPCjiPqHvkQ6J2GWTw":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, ('MISSING: '+old[:90])\n    s=s.replace(old,new,1)\n\n# --- 6.2 boot: replace the code block and the first bullets\na=s.index(\"### 6.2 Boot in a session\")\nb=s.index(\"- Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"### 6.2 Boot in