{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD6wJpiLXhz7dpuSZn7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The literal recipes render the same picture on WebGPU and on the WebGL2 fallback. I'll apply the last small notes from this check and write the exit interview."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2694,"cache_read_input_tokens":430454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2694},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"a12ceb97-191f-4691-86ea-0c9b028283ec","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:50.534Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD6v3fKTH8xmo8ewaFh"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD6wJpiLXhz7dpuSZn7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QX6kUrf4FXvutWGsWcAJax","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, ('MISSING: '+old[:90])\n    s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nrep(\"// Smoke: the same card with the same billboard (w grows with height, stacked in rising columns):\",\n    \"// Smoke: the same card, smokeMat.positionNode = fireMat.positionNode, the same attribute name, w growing with height, in rising columns:\")\nrep(\"### 13.4 Rendering recipes (✔ all verified, copy them)\\n\",\n    \"### 13.4 Rendering recipes (✔ all verified, copy them)\\n\\n✔ The planner extracted the code blocks below from this file as written, ran them, and got the target image on WebGPU and the same picture on the WebGL2 fallback.\\n\")\nrep(\"✔ With three and Rapier inlined, this came to 3.1 MB, opens on `file://`, makes no network requests, and passes the harness when served. Inline everything; no CDN.\",\n    \"✔ With three and Rapier inlined, this came to 3.1 MB, opens on `file://`, makes no network requests, and passes the harness when served. Inline everything; no CDN. A `<script type=\\\"module\\\" src=…>` won't load on `file://` at all (✔ blocked), so test builds are inlined too.\")\nrep(\"- Boots with no page errors or console errors (the Rapier `console.warn` is fine).\",\n    \"- Boots with no page errors or console errors (`console.warn` is fine: Rapier's init notice, and on the fallback three's \\\"running under WebGL2\\\" and ANGLE's ReadPixels notes).\")\nrep(\"- The \\\"This computer\\\" section of your TASK.md still applies. §14.1 lists where the planner found it needs a correction.\",\n    \"- The \\\"This computer\\\" section of your TASK.md still applies. §14.1 lists where the planner found it needs a correction.\\n- **Map of this file:** 1 the game, 2 world, 3 loop and pacing, 4 systems, 5 story, 6 multiplayer, 7 UI, 8 attract, 9 dev mode, 10 art, 11 animation, 12 audio, 13 tech and recipes, 14 testing, 15 build order, 16 done checklist.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > planner-exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"It separates what is fixed from what is mine to decide, and backs the fixed parts with things I could run. Genre, perspective, fiction and scope were open. The tech stack, the 10-foot rules, the attract mode and the music level were firm. The AI Hub harness and the 'This computer' section meant I could test claims before writing them down instead of guessing. Leaving the title and file names to each builder also kept the plan on what matters: the game.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was confusing?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Three things. (1) 'Follow [the hub page] for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own' can mean either 'the game must still run outside a session' or 'it must also have multiplayer outside a session'. I planned for both: co-op through the hub, plus a same-computer link when there is no hub. (2) TASK.md says Chromium has software WebGPU with three flags, and treats a blank canvas as a screenshot limitation. On this machine those flags give an adapter, but the device is destroyed on the first canvas frame, so nothing draws and no JS error appears. It took several experiments to find this. The hub's own documented flags, which add --use-vulkan=swiftshader and --use-angle=swiftshader, give real pixels and working screenshots. (3) TASK.md is written to the builder, so as the planner I had to work out which parts applied to me. I treated the Source Information, the exit interview and the testing rules as the builder's and only planned for them. 'The engine's asset library' is also vague for three.js: the npm package ships no models, only geometry helpers and fonts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Finding the right size for a plan that someone else must finish alone. It has to be specific enough to build without me and capture what makes Far Cry 2 distinctive, while being an original world, cast, map and story rather than a reskin. It also has to fit one builder of unknown model and budget, which is why it has a build order and a table of what may shrink and what may not. The hardest technical part was getting a 3D game through the hub's checks under software rendering. All harness copies share one main thread, and even a small skeleton that rendered while loading failed the hub's default no-flags run at four copies. Sending hello early, calling ready before the renderer, drawing no 3D frame before start and throttling slow frames fixed it, but I only learned that by running it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"(1) Correct the WebGPU flags in 'This computer' to the set that draws, and say that a blank canvas with those flags means a lost device, not a screenshot limit. (2) Add a note that the long TMPDIR makes full Chromium abort with 'Socket path too long', so only the headless shell works unless TMPDIR is shortened. (3) Say plainly whether standalone multiplayer is required, and if so, whether a same-computer link is enough. (4) Warn that hub harness copies share one main thread and that the hub's default check runs without WebGPU, because that decides the boot order. (5) Tell the planner roughly how much budget and which model the builder will have, since scope is the planner's biggest decision and I had to guess. (6) In STAGE.md, say which TASK.md sections are for the builder only, and whether the planner should leave its experiments behind or clean them up.\"\n  }\n]\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json'))\nprint(len(d),[x['question'] for x in d])\nassert [x['question'] for x in d]==['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','What would you change in this prompt?']\n\"; grep -n -i -E \"exit-interview\\.json|GameTitle|claude-opus|20261104|HARNESS_CLAIM\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-140; ls -la","description":"Apply final notes, write the exit interview, validate JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2694,"cache_read_input_tokens":430454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2694},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0178d0d-15a3-488a-af93-32cb0d078d37","uuid":"a6c6a058-1a43-4474-b4ed-7531ee75efab","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:14:10.757Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD6v3fKTH8xmo8ewaFh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QX6kUrf4FXvutWGsWcAJax":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, ('MISSING: '+old[:90])\n    s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nrep(\"// Smoke: the same card with the same billboard (w grows with height, stacked in rising columns):\",\n    \"// Smoke: the same card, smokeMat.positionNode = fireMat.positionNode, the same attribute name, w growing with height, in rising columns:\")\nrep(\"### 13.4 Rendering recipes (✔ all verified, copy them)\\n\",\n    \"### 13.4 Rendering recipes (✔ all verified, copy them)\\n\\n✔ The planner extracted the code blocks below from this file as written, ran them, and got the target image on WebGPU and the same picture on the WebGL2 fallback.\\n\")\nrep(\"✔ With three and Rapier inlined, this came 