1) Correct the WebGPU flags in 'This computer' to the set that draws, and say that a blank canvas with those flags means a lost device, not a screenshot limit. (2) Add a note that the long TMPDIR makes full Chromium abort with 'Socket path too long', so only the headless shell works unless TMPDIR is shortened. (3) Say plainly whether standalone multiplayer is required, and if so, whether a same-computer link is enough. (4) Warn that hub harness copies share one main thread and that the hub's default check runs without WebGPU, because that decides the boot order. (5) Tell the planner roughly how much budget and which model the builder will have, since scope is the planner's biggest decision and I had to guess. (6) In STAGE.md, say which TASK.md sections are for the builder only, and whether the planner should leave its experiments behind or clean them up.\"\n  }\n]\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json'))\nprint(len(d),[x['question'] for x in d])\nassert [x['question'] for x in d]==['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','What would you change in this prompt?']\n\"; grep -n -i -E \"exit-interview\\.json|GameTitle|claude-opus|20261104|HARNESS_CLAIM\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-140; ls -la","description":"Apply final notes, write the exit interview, validate JSON"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01QX6kUrf4FXvutWGsWcAJax":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211935__x12d0e8/work"}}}
